window.CARDS=window.CARDS||{};CARDS["people-ibuki-mio"]=[{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p78-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka yamauchi-haruki hirata-yousuke kushida-kikyou ibuki-mio","q":"ibuki mio ch 2 sec  2 6 sec  2 8  the class c girl with the swollen cheek a path in the forest on the way back to camp  she sits against a large tree  not a class d student  with a red  swollen mark on her cheek   just a class dispute  don t worry about it    her answer when asked who did it   her voice was low and even  but it was clear she wasn t feeling well  names the barrier herself   i m from class c  in other words  i m your enemy  you understand that  right  refuses the base camp offer    there s no way i could do something like that    then watches them refuse to leave   you guys are really stupid  you re not acting logically  you aren t thinking about your own class  introductions after the standoff   i m ibuki    and she won t meet his eyes  dirt under her nails and disturbed soil where she sat   the page shows the fight without naming who won it  the account  once hirata s offer sticks   i had a fight with a boy in my class  he hit me and chased me away  that s all  on his decency   he s seriously a good natured guy  isn t he    and the class c verdict   not at all  there isn t really anyone in class c like that  gets kushida s group ration    are you guys stupid  you re all being way too nice    and is told to eat first  talk later  told to wait while the class decides  the class agrees to shelter her once roll call attrition makes it profitable  not only decent","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p78-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 sec. 2.6–sec. 2.8: the Class C girl with the swollen cheek<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.78–96<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">A path in the forest on the way back to camp; she sits against a large tree, not a Class D student, with a red, swollen mark on her cheek.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"yamauchi-haruki.html\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/a> · <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> &quot;Just a class dispute. Don’t worry about it&quot; — her answer when asked who did it; &quot;her voice was low and even, but it was clear she wasn’t feeling well.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.80<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Names the barrier herself: “I’m from Class C. In other words, I’m your enemy. You understand that, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.81<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/b> Refuses the base-camp offer — &quot;There’s no way I could do something like that&quot; — then watches them refuse to leave: &quot;You guys are really stupid. You’re not acting logically. You aren’t thinking about your own class.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.81–82<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Introductions after the standoff: “I’m…Ibuki” — and she won&#x27;t meet his eyes.<span class=\"pg\">p.82<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> Dirt under her nails and disturbed soil where she sat — the page shows the fight without naming who won it.<span class=\"pg\">p.82<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> The account, once Hirata&#x27;s offer sticks: &quot;I had a fight with a boy in my class. He hit me and chased me away. That’s all.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.94–95<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> On his decency: “He’s seriously a good-natured guy, isn’t he?” — and the Class C verdict: &quot;Not at all… There isn’t really anyone in Class C like that.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.95<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Gets Kushida&#x27;s group ration — &quot;Are you guys stupid? You’re all being way too nice.&quot; — and is told to eat first, talk later.<span class=\"pg\">p.96<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Told to wait while the class decides; the class agrees to shelter her once roll-call attrition makes it profitable, not only decent.<span class=\"pg\">p.91<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p100-1\">→ After: Ch.3: the camera in her bag<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p100-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"","w":"ibuki-mio","q":"ibuki mio ch 3  the camera in her bag the luggage pile outside the tent before dawn  her singularly colored bag is easy to spot  her rented digital camera   no data  no sign it was ever used   is found in the bag while she sleeps and put back untouched","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p100-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3: the camera in her bag<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.100<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The luggage pile outside the tent before dawn; her singularly colored bag is easy to spot.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Her rented digital camera — no data, no sign it was ever used — is found in the bag while she sleeps and put back untouched.<span class=\"pg\">p.100<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p78-1\">← Before: Ch.2 sec. 2.6–sec. 2.8: the Class C girl with the swollen cheek<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p105-1\">→ After: Ch.3 sec. 3.1: the visit to the campsite<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p105-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"spoken","w":"ryuuen-kakeru ibuki-mio","q":"ibuki mio ch 3 sec  3 1  the visit to the campsite class c s boys stride into the campsite  a pained expression flashes across her face and she ducks behind the tent to hide   do you know ryuuen  sounds irritated discussing him    as if she were discussing a family enemy  komiya and kondou are his underlings  his name alone puts her behind the tent   i don t think they were looking for me   i wonder if things are heading toward that worst case scenario i imagined","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p105-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3 sec. 3.1: the visit to the campsite<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.105–106<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Class C&#x27;s boys stride into the campsite; a pained expression flashes across her face and she ducks behind the tent to hide.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Do you know Ryuuen?”<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I don&#x27;t think they were looking for me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.106<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I wonder if things are heading toward that worst-case scenario I imagined…”<span class=\"pg\">p.106<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Sounds irritated discussing him — “as if she were discussing a family enemy.”<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Komiya and Kondou are his underlings; his name alone puts her behind the tent.<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p100-1\">← Before: Ch.3: the camera in her bag<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p171-1\">→ After: Ch.6 sec. 6.1: the new suspect<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p171-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"","w":"ibuki-mio","q":"ibuki mio ch 6 sec  6 1  the new suspect sitting at the far edge of the camp  she becomes the class s new prey the moment someone says her name  the collective s doubts swing to her instantly  she is the outsider from class c   hey  what if it was that girl  ibuki  and the sabotage theory that follows are left untagged in the translation","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p171-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 sec. 6.1: the new suspect<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.171–178<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Sitting at the far edge of the camp, she becomes the class’s new prey the moment someone says her name.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> The collective’s doubts swing to her instantly; she is the outsider from Class C.<span class=\"pg\">p.178<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> “Hey. What if it was that girl, Ibuki?” and the sabotage theory that follows are left untagged in the translation.<span class=\"pg\">p.178<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p105-1\">← Before: Ch.3 sec. 3.1: the visit to the campsite<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p181-1\">→ After: Ch.6 sec. 6.2: the test<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p181-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka ibuki-mio","q":"ibuki mio ch 6 sec  6 2  the test walks up to ayanokoji alone after the morning s accusations and tests whether he suspects her   do you have a minute   what you were talking about this morning sounded really serious  the   underwear incident  i mean  i mean  class d isn t a monolith  yamauchi had taken her in  and kushida s group was looking after her   no particular reason to seek him out   whatever the reason  stealing a girl s underwear is unforgivable   do you doubt me  by any chance   are you the culprit   okay  that s good  well  it s not like i had any evidence or anything  it looks like some of the girls trust you and that boy hirata  i think the chance of you being a villain is low   do you have any idea who the culprit is   so who do you think did it  asks as if she were testing him  glancing at him out of the corner of her eye   if a boy isn t the culprit  then they ll suspect me the stranger next  i m absolutely certain some people have already said something about me  after all  i could ve just made it look like the guys stole the underwear  right   thank you  i didn t think you would say something like that  he says he trusts her while his own narration names her the culprit","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p181-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 sec. 6.2: the test<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.181–183<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Walks up to Ayanokōji alone after the morning’s accusations and tests whether he suspects her.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Do you have a minute?”<span class=\"pg\">p.181<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“What you were talking about this morning sounded really serious. The … underwear incident, I mean. I mean, Class D isn’t a monolith.”<span class=\"pg\">p.181<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Whatever the reason, stealing a girl’s underwear is unforgivable.”<span class=\"pg\">p.182<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>10 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Yamauchi had taken her in, and Kushida’s group was looking after her — no particular reason to seek him out.<span class=\"pg\">p.182<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Do you doubt me, by any chance?”<span class=\"pg\">p.182<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Are you the culprit?”<span class=\"pg\">p.182<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Okay, that’s good. Well, it’s not like I had any evidence or anything. It looks like some of the girls trust you and that boy Hirata. I think the chance of you being a villain is low.”<span class=\"pg\">p.182<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Do you have any idea who the culprit is?”<span class=\"pg\">p.182<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So who do you think did it?”<span class=\"pg\">p.182<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Asks as if she were testing him, glancing at him out of the corner of her eye.<span class=\"pg\">p.182<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If a boy isn’t the culprit, then they’ll suspect me—the stranger—next. I’m absolutely certain some people have already said something about me. After all, I could’ve just made it look like the guys stole the underwear. Right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.182<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Thank you. I didn’t think you would say something like that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.183<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> He says he trusts her while his own narration names her the culprit.<span class=\"pg\">p.183<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p171-1\">← Before: Ch.6 sec. 6.1: the new suspect<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p194-1\">→ After: Ch.6 sec. 6.4: joining the search<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p194-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action spoken","w":"kushida-kikyou ibuki-mio","q":"ibuki mio ch 6 sec  6 4  joining the search invited along on the last forage  she agrees out of a debt to class d   okay  i owe class d a debt of gratitude  sure  i ll help  slings her bag over her shoulder and steps into the forest with the group  paired with kushida for the search   the last two left once the others split","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p194-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 sec. 6.4: joining the search<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.194–199<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Invited along on the last forage, she agrees out of a debt to Class D.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Okay. I owe Class D a debt of gratitude… Sure, I’ll help.”<span class=\"pg\">p.194<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Slings her bag over her shoulder and steps into the forest with the group.<span class=\"pg\">p.194<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Paired with Kushida for the search — the last two left once the others split.<span class=\"pg\">p.197<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p181-1\">← Before: Ch.6 sec. 6.2: the test<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p201-1\">→ After: Ch.6 sec. 6.5: the shower line<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p201-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action spoken","w":"sakura-airi ibuki-mio","q":"ibuki mio ch 6 sec  6 5  the shower line waits out the river swim in the shower queue   the line position that will later clear karuizawa  and place her   i ll pass  i don t really like swimming  so i ll just wait to use the shower room  takes the tail of the line behind karuizawa s group and sakura  sakura follows her lead in refusing the swim  the two wait in line together   whoa  looks like it s moving now","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p201-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 sec. 6.5: the shower line<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.201–202<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Waits out the river swim in the shower queue — the line position that will later clear Karuizawa, and place her.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“I’ll pass. I don’t really like swimming, so I’ll just wait to use the shower room,”<span class=\"pg\">p.201<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Whoa, looks like it’s moving now.”<span class=\"pg\">p.202<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Takes the tail of the line behind Karuizawa’s group and Sakura.<span class=\"pg\">p.202<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> Sakura follows her lead in refusing the swim; the two wait in line together.<span class=\"pg\">p.202<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p194-1\">← Before: Ch.6 sec. 6.4: joining the search<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p206-1\">→ After: Ch.6 sec. 6.7: the fire she did not set<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p206-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action","w":"horikita-suzune ibuki-mio","q":"ibuki mio ch 6 sec  6 7  the fire she did not set stands at the burning bundle wearing such genuine confusion that horikita hesitates to call her over  held as the likeliest culprit by horikita   and watched being surprised by a fire she insists later she did not start  slips away with one of the bags while suspicion turns on her","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p206-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 sec. 6.7: the fire she did not set<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.206–208<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Stands at the burning bundle wearing such genuine confusion that Horikita hesitates to call her over.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q action\">Slips away with one of the bags while suspicion turns on her.<span class=\"pg\">p.208<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Held as the likeliest culprit by Horikita — and watched being surprised by a fire she insists later she did not start.<span class=\"pg\">p.206<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p201-1\">← Before: Ch.6 sec. 6.5: the shower line<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p213-1\">→ After: Ch.6 sec. 6.8: cornered in the rain<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p213-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action spoken","w":"horikita-suzune ibuki-mio","q":"ibuki mio ch 6 sec  6 8  cornered in the rain waits in the mud knowing horikita is behind her  then turns and talks her in circles until the fight starts   what are you doing  horikita   when did you notice me   right from the start   why were you following me   do you really not know   no  i don t know   you clearly know why i was following you  don t you   i really have no idea what you re talking about   why should i lie   i d at least like to hear why you followed me  from your own lips   the underwear theft and the fire  misfortune continues to befall class d   so what   do you realize that some people suspect you   ah  i suppose since i m an outsider  there s not much i can do about that   that s what i m talking about   you re saying i m the culprit  do you have any proof   unfortunately  i don t have a single shred of evidence related to the underwear theft  but i think it was you   that s a pretty terrible thing to say  you don t have any evidence  yet you suspect me  as horikita assesses her  laid low since day five  kept her distance from class d  and   contrary to expectations   was not suspected   i suspect you because of today  you don t need me to explain that  do you   let me cut to the chase  i want you to return something you took from me   i don t know what you re talking about   where are you going   who knows   how long are you going to follow me  don t you think enough is enough   once you return what you stole from me   why don t you calm down and try thinking  if i stole the keycard  would i have held onto it  if someone saw me with it  that would mean immediate disqualification  i d only end up losing points myself  right  lets the word  keycard  slip when horikita never said it   the confession by mistake the narration catches for her   you thought i confessed to something  didn t you  you re wrong   i m tired of talking with you  digs in the ground with both hands while horikita falters against a tree   your condition has gotten a lot worse  hasn t it   ibuki san  i m going to investigate you with everything i ve got  you don t mind   with everything you ve got  could you be a bit more specific  you mean you re going to resort to violence   my last warning  huh  oh  i get it  i get it  why don t you get your wish  drops the bag and raises her arms as if surrendering   and kicks the moment horikita reaches for it   oh  you re good   someone might see us here  you mean  weren t you willing to use violence  too  grabs horikita s shoulders and throws her into the mud  sneering from above   would you like a moment to rest   oh  you can really move  surprisingly  you practice or something  sizes horikita s martial arts up without panic and enjoys the exchange   white teeth showing the whole while   you ve been trying really hard until now  i ll tell you the truth  as a reward  i stole the card  draws the card out of her pocket and shows the engraved name   you gave up the truth pretty easily   it doesn t matter if i admit it or not now  there s no evidence i used violence against you  it s not as though the school can make a judgment here  isn t that right   involved  in what   i didn t burn the manual  the denial comes out after a hesitation   she stole the card but insists the fire was not hers   you intend to keep lying even now   what would i gain by burning it  it was inevitable that people would begin searching for the criminal after the uproar  besides  people would suspect me rather strongly  there was nothing to gain and a lot to lose   i don t understand  i thought you were involved   do you think he s in class d  there s a guy who figured me out before you did  she leaves the man unnamed  the page names no one   so  you can t mean   this conversation is over  ends the talk with a blow to the head  sweeps her leg  slaps her cheek  and kicks her in the face on the last try to rise   do you think they ll permit such coercive methods   come on  now  i don t feel like answering that","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p213-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 sec. 6.8: cornered in the rain<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.213–220<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Waits in the mud knowing Horikita is behind her, then turns and talks her in circles until the fight starts.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“What are you doing, Horikita?”<span class=\"pg\">p.213<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “When did you notice me?”<span class=\"pg\">p.213<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Right from the start.”<span class=\"pg\">p.213<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>56 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Why were you following me?”<span class=\"pg\">p.213<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Do you really not know?”<span class=\"pg\">p.213<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No, I don’t know.”<span class=\"pg\">p.213<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You clearly know why I was following you, don’t you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.213<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I really have no idea what you’re talking about.”<span class=\"pg\">p.213<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Why should I lie?”<span class=\"pg\">p.213<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’d at least like to hear why you followed me, from your own lips.”<span class=\"pg\">p.213<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The underwear theft and the fire. Misfortune continues to befall Class D.”<span class=\"pg\">p.214<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So what?”<span class=\"pg\">p.214<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Do you realize that some people suspect you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.214<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ah. I suppose since I’m an outsider, there’s not much I can do about that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.214<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s what I’m talking about.”<span class=\"pg\">p.214<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re saying I’m the culprit? Do you have any proof?”<span class=\"pg\">p.214<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Unfortunately, I don’t have a single shred of evidence related to the underwear theft. But I think it was you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.214<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s a pretty terrible thing to say. You don’t have any evidence, yet you suspect me?”<span class=\"pg\">p.214<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> As Horikita assesses her: laid low since day five, kept her distance from Class D, and — contrary to expectations — was not suspected.<span class=\"pg\">p.214<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I suspect you because of today. You don’t need me to explain that, do you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.214<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Let me cut to the chase. I want you to return something you took from me,”<span class=\"pg\">p.214<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t know what you’re talking about.”<span class=\"pg\">p.214<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Where are you going?”<span class=\"pg\">p.214<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Who knows?”<span class=\"pg\">p.214<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “How long are you going to follow me? Don’t you think enough is enough?”<span class=\"pg\">p.215<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Once you return what you stole from me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.215<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Why don’t you calm down and try thinking? If I stole the keycard, would I have held onto it? If someone saw me with it, that would mean immediate disqualification. I’d only end up losing points myself, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.215<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Lets the word “keycard” slip when Horikita never said it — the confession by mistake the narration catches for her.<span class=\"pg\">p.215<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You thought I confessed to something, didn’t you? You’re wrong.”<span class=\"pg\">p.215<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m tired of talking with you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.216<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Digs in the ground with both hands while Horikita falters against a tree.<span class=\"pg\">p.216<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Your condition has gotten a lot worse, hasn’t it?”<span class=\"pg\">p.216<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ibuki-san. I’m going to investigate you with everything I’ve got. You don’t mind?”<span class=\"pg\">p.216<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “With everything you’ve got? Could you be a bit more specific? You mean you’re going to resort to violence?”<span class=\"pg\">p.216<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “My last warning, huh? Oh, I get it. I get it. Why don’t you get your wish?”<span class=\"pg\">p.216<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Drops the bag and raises her arms as if surrendering — and kicks the moment Horikita reaches for it.<span class=\"pg\">p.216<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Oh, you’re good,”<span class=\"pg\">p.217<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Someone might see us here, you mean? Weren’t you willing to use violence, too?”<span class=\"pg\">p.217<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Grabs Horikita’s shoulders and throws her into the mud, sneering from above.<span class=\"pg\">p.217<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Would you like a moment to rest?”<span class=\"pg\">p.217<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Oh? You can really move, surprisingly. You practice or something?”<span class=\"pg\">p.217<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Sizes Horikita’s martial arts up without panic and enjoys the exchange — white teeth showing the whole while.<span class=\"pg\">p.218<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’ve been trying really hard until now. I’ll tell you the truth, as a reward. I stole the card.”<span class=\"pg\">p.218<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Draws the card out of her pocket and shows the engraved name.<span class=\"pg\">p.218<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You gave up the truth pretty easily.”<span class=\"pg\">p.218<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It doesn’t matter if I admit it or not now. There’s no evidence I used violence against you. It’s not as though the school can make a judgment here. Isn’t that right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.218<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Involved? In what?”<span class=\"pg\">p.219<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I didn’t burn the manual.”<span class=\"pg\">p.219<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The denial comes out after a hesitation — she stole the card but insists the fire was not hers.<span class=\"pg\">p.219<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You intend to keep lying even now?”<span class=\"pg\">p.219<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What would I gain by burning it? It was inevitable that people would begin searching for the criminal after the uproar. Besides, people would suspect me rather strongly. There was nothing to gain and a lot to lose.”<span class=\"pg\">p.219<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t understand… I thought you were involved.”<span class=\"pg\">p.219<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Do you think he’s in Class D? There’s a guy who figured me out before you did.”<span class=\"pg\">p.220<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> She leaves the man unnamed; the page names no one.<span class=\"pg\">p.220<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So. You can’t mean…”<span class=\"pg\">p.220<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “This conversation is over.”<span class=\"pg\">p.220<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Ends the talk with a blow to the head, sweeps her leg, slaps her cheek, and kicks her in the face on the last try to rise.<span class=\"pg\">p.220<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Do you think they’ll permit such coercive methods?”<span class=\"pg\">p.220<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Come on, now. I don’t feel like answering that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.220<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p206-1\">← Before: Ch.6 sec. 6.7: the fire she did not set<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p221-1\">→ After: Ch.6 sec. 6.9: the handover<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p221-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action inner spoken","w":"ryuuen-kakeru katsuragi-kouhei horikita-suzune ibuki-mio","q":"ibuki mio ch 6 sec  6 9  the handover her viewpoint  she stands over the unconscious horikita  digs up the flashlight and transceiver  and calls her leader in   what   is it because of the rain  the buried items seem slightly different from when she hid them   her own doubt  unresolved on the page  reports her location over the transceiver and waits half an hour for his blinking flashlight   yo  excellent work  ibuki  you did well   naturally  yes   naturally  if you hadn t made any mistakes until now  i wouldn t have had to risk coming over here   that couldn t be helped  i hadn t planned for the digital camera to break  the camera s breaking forced her to carry the card instead of photographing it   the risk that let horikita catch her   so  where s the card   it s here  hands the card over  ryuuen checks the engraved name under his flashlight  watches him come out of the shadows to inspect the card under the condition he set   you come over here and confirm it  too  that was your condition  remember  relax  it s dark out  and this weather is horrible  there shouldn t be anyone here  it s great to be cautious  but don t waste time   it looks like the real thing   you managed to infiltrate class d quite well  weren t you suspected  the question carries no speaker tag  it follows his inspection of the card and her methods  so it is recorded as his   under normal circumstances  i would have been  but as for my methods  that s a trade secret  the spying operation from the test s start  ryuuen slapped her to make the lie true  and class d read her as beaten and chased out of her class   don t sit there and think about it forever  the situation is black and white  so make your decision  you re already halfway there  don t do something as stupid as pulling out here   you re right  the assent is untagged  it sits under ryuuen s pressure  and the narration still reads him as not having consented   if this wasn t an honorable deed  then what are you going to do  did you know that sakayanagi s faction has dominated ever since rumors spread that you failed to get on the student council despite your best efforts  this might be your chance  right   you bastard  why are you telling me this   class a maintains its position by forming alliances  if you can form those  even those who have double crossed you will return under your wing  won t they  or you could make me your enemy  i suppose  if you do  i wonder what would happen   sakayanagi is absent  it s impossible for someone indecisive to rule class a   we ve established negotiations  as promised  i accept your proposal   that s good  you ve exercised sound judgment   wait  what negotiation  would you explain   to form an alliance  with class a   i ll be heading back now  i don t want to risk things by lingering for too long  watches katsuragi return the card and disappear into the darkness   what about the negotiation  what was discussed  what are we getting in return   but is there any guarantee katsuragi will keep his promise  he might renege  the doubt and the answer that follows both run untagged  the answer is recorded as ryuuen s   i have that covered  of course  he will have no choice but to honor his promise  lays out the contract s terms to her with a creepy smile   the page never quotes them   everything was going according to ryuuen s plan  including the fact that most of our students had retired   he was probably the man with abilities closest to those of class a  after all  i had to acknowledge it  wipes her fingerprints from the card and sticks it back in horikita s hand  reads her as no threat   untrusting  unreported  enduring in silence   and leaves the card with her   use your smarts to protect yourself  says it to the unconscious horikita  then disappears with ryuuen into the dark woods","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p221-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 sec. 6.9: the handover<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.221–224<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Her viewpoint: she stands over the unconscious Horikita, digs up the flashlight and transceiver, and calls her leader in.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“What?”<span class=\"pg\">p.221<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Is it because of the rain?”<span class=\"pg\">p.221<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> “Yo. Excellent work, Ibuki. You did well.”<span class=\"pg\">p.221<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>40 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The buried items seem slightly different from when she hid them — her own doubt, unresolved on the page.<span class=\"pg\">p.221<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Reports her location over the transceiver and waits half an hour for his blinking flashlight.<span class=\"pg\">p.221<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Naturally, yes?”<span class=\"pg\">p.221<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Naturally? If you hadn’t made any mistakes until now, I wouldn’t have had to risk coming over here.”<span class=\"pg\">p.221<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That couldn’t be helped. I hadn’t planned for the digital camera to break.”<span class=\"pg\">p.221<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The camera’s breaking forced her to carry the card instead of photographing it — the risk that let Horikita catch her.<span class=\"pg\">p.221<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So, where’s the card?”<span class=\"pg\">p.222<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s here.”<span class=\"pg\">p.222<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Hands the card over; Ryuuen checks the engraved name under his flashlight.<span class=\"pg\">p.222<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> Watches him come out of the shadows to inspect the card under the condition he set.<span class=\"pg\">p.222<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You come over here and confirm it, too. That was your condition, remember? Relax, it’s dark out, and this weather is horrible. There shouldn’t be anyone here. It’s great to be cautious, but don’t waste time.”<span class=\"pg\">p.222<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It looks like the real thing,”<span class=\"pg\">p.222<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You managed to infiltrate Class D quite well. Weren’t you suspected?”<span class=\"pg\">p.222<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The question carries no speaker tag; it follows his inspection of the card and her methods, so it is recorded as his.<span class=\"pg\">p.222<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Under normal circumstances, I would have been. But as for my methods, that’s a trade secret.”<span class=\"pg\">p.222<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Backstory<\/span> The spying operation from the test’s start: Ryuuen slapped her to make the lie true, and Class D read her as beaten and chased out of her class.<span class=\"pg\">p.222<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Don’t sit there and think about it forever. The situation is black-and-white, so make your decision. You’re already halfway there. Don’t do something as stupid as pulling out here.”<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re right.”<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The assent is untagged; it sits under Ryuuen’s pressure, and the narration still reads him as not having consented.<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If this wasn’t an honorable deed, then what are you going to do? Did you know that Sakayanagi’s faction has dominated ever since rumors spread that you failed to get on the student council despite your best efforts? This might be your chance, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You bastard. Why are you telling me this?”<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Class A maintains its position by forming alliances. If you can form those, even those who have double-crossed you will return under your wing, won’t they? Or you could make me your enemy, I suppose? If you do, I wonder what would happen?”<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Sakayanagi is absent. It’s impossible for someone indecisive to rule Class A.”<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “We’ve established negotiations, as promised. I accept your proposal.”<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s good. You’ve exercised sound judgment.”<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Wait, what negotiation? Would you explain?”<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “To form an alliance. With Class A.”<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ll be heading back now. I don’t want to risk things by lingering for too long.”<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Watches Katsuragi return the card and disappear into the darkness.<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What about the negotiation? What was discussed? What are we getting in return?”<span class=\"pg\">p.224<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But…is there any guarantee Katsuragi will keep his promise? He might renege.”<span class=\"pg\">p.224<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The doubt and the answer that follows both run untagged; the answer is recorded as Ryuuen’s.<span class=\"pg\">p.224<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I have that covered, of course. He will have no choice but to honor his promise.”<span class=\"pg\">p.224<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Lays out the contract’s terms to her with a creepy smile — the page never quotes them.<span class=\"pg\">p.224<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> “Everything was going according to Ryuuen’s plan, including the fact that most of our students had retired.”<span class=\"pg\">p.224<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> “he was probably the man with abilities closest to those of Class A, after all. I had to acknowledge it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.224<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Wipes her fingerprints from the card and sticks it back in Horikita’s hand.<span class=\"pg\">p.224<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Reads her as no threat — untrusting, unreported, enduring in silence — and leaves the card with her.<span class=\"pg\">p.224<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Use your smarts to protect yourself.”<span class=\"pg\">p.224<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Says it to the unconscious Horikita, then disappears with Ryuuen into the dark woods.<span class=\"pg\">p.224<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p213-1\">← Before: Ch.6 sec. 6.8: cornered in the rain<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p241-1\">→ After: Ch.7: the culprit named<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p241-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"spoken","w":"karuizawa-kei horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka ryuuen-kakeru ibuki-mio","q":"ibuki mio ch 7  the culprit named named everywhere she is absent   the emptied beach  karuizawa s apology  and the lounge retelling that finally explains how her theft fit a larger plan  nowhere on the sandy beach when the class c camp is found emptied  as if she d retired as well   ibuki san stole my underwear  ayanokouji kun told us everything  the culprit karuizawa names to her face  the chase and collapse of the sixth day are what the apology is about   horikita san  when you noticed that ibuki san was the culprit  she tried to run because you questioned her  right  that s why you ended up collapsing and getting sick   but wait  ibuki san stole my card  but what if i d protected it really thoroughly   did you drop the card on purpose back then  well  i suppose that yamauchi kun s actions might have provided ibuki san the opportunity to hatch a plan to steal the keycard  ibuki was picked up by class d  but not by chance   the near coincidence of two people saved by two separate classes dissolved once kaneda in class b came out as a spy ryuuen had sent  the bigger the lie  the more obvious the habit   she looked him straight in the eye even over the underwear theft  the one who read her eye contact habit and her camera plan  ibuki carried a digital camera to take a picture of the keycard  a photo would have made the leader s identity clear to anyone and let her profit  his spy on the island   the card  the camera and the transceiver all served the plan  and people outside class c wanted her evidence rather than her word  ibuki hiding a wireless transceiver in the ground proved someone was left on the island for her to contact  ryuuen set it on a table unguarded while on vacation   no one else controlled it  and his mistake was trusting no one","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p241-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.7: the culprit named<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.241–256<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named everywhere she is absent — the emptied beach, Karuizawa’s apology, and the lounge retelling that finally explains how her theft fit a larger plan.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> “Ibuki-san stole my underwear. Ayanokouji-kun told us everything.”<span class=\"pg\">p.246<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> “Horikita-san, when you noticed that Ibuki-san was the culprit, she tried to run because you questioned her, right? That’s why you ended up collapsing and getting sick…”<span class=\"pg\">p.247<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “But wait. Ibuki-san stole my card, but what if I’d protected it really thoroughly?”<span class=\"pg\">p.254<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Nowhere on the sandy beach when the Class C camp is found emptied, as if she’d retired as well.<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> The culprit Karuizawa names to her face; the chase and collapse of the sixth day are what the apology is about.<span class=\"pg\">p.246–247<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Did you drop the card on purpose back then? Well, I suppose that Yamauchi-kun’s actions might have provided Ibuki-san the opportunity to hatch a plan to steal the keycard…”<span class=\"pg\">p.254<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Fact<\/span> Ibuki was picked up by Class D, but not by chance — the near-coincidence of two people saved by two separate classes dissolved once Kaneda in Class B came out as a spy Ryuuen had sent.<span class=\"pg\">p.255<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The bigger the lie, the more obvious the habit — she looked him straight in the eye even over the underwear theft.<span class=\"pg\">p.255<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> The one who read her eye-contact habit and her camera plan.<span class=\"pg\">p.255<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Fact<\/span> Ibuki carried a digital camera to take a picture of the keycard; a photo would have made the leader’s identity clear to anyone and let her profit.<span class=\"pg\">p.255<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> His spy on the island — the card, the camera and the transceiver all served the plan, and people outside Class C wanted her evidence rather than her word.<span class=\"pg\">p.255–256<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Fact<\/span> Ibuki hiding a wireless transceiver in the ground proved someone was left on the island for her to contact; Ryuuen set it on a table unguarded while on vacation — no one else controlled it, and his mistake was trusting no one.<span class=\"pg\">p.256<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p221-1\">← Before: Ch.6 sec. 6.9: the handover<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4-p16-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"ibuki-mio","q":"ibuki mio ch 2 sec  2 0  a passing mention as the culprit named once as the underwear culprit  ayanokoji asks whether karuizawa got hers back  hirata confirms the fallout  naming her resolved things    when she heard ibuki san was the culprit  things went smoothly","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4-p16-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 sec. 2.0: a passing mention as the culprit<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.16<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named once as the underwear culprit; Ayanokōji asks whether Karuizawa got hers back.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Hirata confirms the fallout: naming her resolved things — “When she heard Ibuki-san was the culprit, things went smoothly.”<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4-p39-1\">→ After: Ch.2: named on the Rabbit roster<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4-p39-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"ibuki-mio","q":"ibuki mio ch 2  named on the rabbit roster the rabbit group roster prints her name among class c s four  listed as ibuki mio with manabe shiho  yabu nanami  and yamashita saki  ayanokoji notes he knows ichinose from class b and ibuki from class c   teammates now","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4-p39-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2: named on the Rabbit roster<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.39<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The Rabbit group roster prints her name among Class C’s four.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Listed as Ibuki Mio with Manabe Shiho, Yabu Nanami, and Yamashita Saki.<span class=\"pg\">p.39<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Ayanokōji notes he knows Ichinose from Class B and Ibuki from Class C — teammates now.<span class=\"pg\">p.39<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4-p16-1\">← Before: Ch.2 sec. 2.0: a passing mention as the culprit<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4-p68-1\">→ After: Ch.3 sec. 3.0–sec. 3.1: the café shadow and the Rabbit holdout<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4-p68-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"ryuuen-kakeru horikita-suzune karuizawa-kei ichinose-honami ibuki-mio","q":"ibuki mio ch 3 sec  3 0 sec  3 1  the cafe shadow and the rabbit holdout walks into blue ocean at ryuen s side as the island spy horikita caught  later sits silent through the whole rabbit first discussion until ichinose calls her name   i m not so stupid that i d let someone like her see through me  things were simply more difficult because of my fever   on losing to horikita   in that case  let s have a rematch  she challenged  closes the distance on horikita ready to lunge  then stops   rules  and ryuen s leash  hold her back   tch  clearly detests working beneath ryuen  yet is exceptionally talented   the precise reason he chose her as the class d spy   so what about sakayanagi  ibuki asked that  not horikita  she wanted to confirm that information herself  apparently  the one question she puts to ryuen all morning  he goes silent before answering  sits  a little further away  as if isolating themselves  in the rabbit circle   same posture as karuizawa  ayanokoji expected a fight with karuizawa over the stolen underwear  ibuki shows no tiredness and no revenge   whatever  i don t really have anything to add  said ibuki  sole class c holdout on the katsuragi no discussion vote   arms crossed since the test began  she does not move and does not speak until called  the others take it as her normal way  his lackey on the reconnaissance walk  she detests the leash but keeps it  the spy she failed against  rematch refused on rules  the girl whose underwear she stole on the island   they share the rabbit room without speaking  answers only when ichinose asks her by name","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4-p68-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3 sec. 3.0–sec. 3.1: the café shadow and the Rabbit holdout<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.68–75, p.88<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Walks into Blue Ocean at Ryūen’s side as the island spy Horikita caught; later sits silent through the whole Rabbit first discussion until Ichinose calls her name.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“I’m not so stupid that I’d let someone like her see through me. Things were simply more difficult because of my fever.” (on losing to Horikita)<span class=\"pg\">p.69<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“In that case, let’s have a rematch,” she challenged.<span class=\"pg\">p.69<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“So what about Sakayanagi?” Ibuki asked that, not Horikita. She wanted to confirm that information herself, apparently.<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>11 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Closes the distance on Horikita ready to lunge, then stops — rules, and Ryūen’s leash, hold her back; “Tch!”<span class=\"pg\">p.69<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Clearly detests working beneath Ryūen, yet is exceptionally talented — the precise reason he chose her as the Class D spy.<span class=\"pg\">p.69<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The one question she puts to Ryūen all morning; he goes silent before answering.<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Sits “a little further away, as if isolating themselves” in the Rabbit circle — same posture as Karuizawa.<span class=\"pg\">p.80<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Ayanokōji expected a fight with Karuizawa over the stolen underwear; Ibuki shows no tiredness and no revenge.<span class=\"pg\">p.80<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Whatever. I don’t really have anything to add,” said Ibuki.<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Sole Class C holdout on the Katsuragi no-discussion vote — arms crossed since the test began, she does not move and does not speak until called; the others take it as her normal way.<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> His lackey on the reconnaissance walk; she detests the leash but keeps it.<span class=\"pg\">p.68–75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> The spy she failed against; rematch refused on rules.<span class=\"pg\">p.68–69<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> The girl whose underwear she stole on the island — they share the Rabbit room without speaking.<span class=\"pg\">p.80, 88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Answers only when Ichinose asks her by name.<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4-p39-1\">← Before: Ch.2: named on the Rabbit roster<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4-p76-1\">→ After: Ch.3: the café shadow<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4-p76-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"ibuki-mio","q":"ibuki mio ch 3  the cafe shadow named in the read of who was watching the cafe meeting  asked whether ibuki san was the culprit of the watch  the answer floats  maybe forced to keep an eye on them  maybe just passing   but she wasn t tired  and she was walking with ryuuen  so she was likely involved","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4-p76-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3: the café shadow<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.76<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named in the read of who was watching the café meeting.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Asked whether Ibuki-san was the culprit of the watch, the answer floats: maybe forced to keep an eye on them, maybe just passing — but she wasn’t tired, and she was walking with Ryuuen, so she was likely involved.<span class=\"pg\">p.76<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4-p68-1\">← Before: Ch.3 sec. 3.0–sec. 3.1: the café shadow and the Rabbit holdout<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4-p94-1\">→ After: Ch.3 sec. 3.1: the outsider’s verdict<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4-p94-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"manabe-shiho karuizawa-kei ibuki-mio","q":"ibuki mio ch 3 sec  3 1  the outsider s verdict watches the manabe karuizawa picture fight from the circle and speaks once  as an outsider   stupid  said ibuki   that s right  this absolutely has nothing to do with me  so i said what i thought as an outsider  crosses her arms and looks away  manabe does not confront her   the narration reads a clear class c hierarchy with ibuki above manabe  looks scornfully over at manabe  showing her contempt  while the other class c girls laugh at karuizawa  above her in the class c pecking order  the only class c voice that does not pile on her","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4-p94-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3 sec. 3.1: the outsider’s verdict<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.94–95<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Watches the Manabe–Karuizawa picture fight from the circle and speaks once, as an outsider.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"manabe-shiho.html\">Manabe Shiho<\/a> · <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Stupid,” said Ibuki.<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“That’s right. This absolutely has nothing to do with me. So I said what I thought as an outsider.”<span class=\"pg\">p.95<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Crosses her arms and looks away; Manabe does not confront her — the narration reads a clear Class C hierarchy with Ibuki above Manabe.<span class=\"pg\">p.95<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Looks scornfully over at Manabe, showing her contempt, while the other Class C girls laugh at Karuizawa.<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Manabe Shiho<\/b> Above her in the Class C pecking order.<span class=\"pg\">p.94–95<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> The only Class C voice that does not pile on her.<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4-p76-1\">← Before: Ch.3: the café shadow<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4-p97-1\">→ After: Ch.3: the holdout and the odd-moves list<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4-p97-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"ibuki-mio","q":"ibuki mio ch 3  the holdout and the odd moves list named as one of the last left in the rabbit room after the first discussion breaks up  the last people in the room are the three class b students and ibuki  appears in ayanokoji s list of things that had been off with horikita since the test began  karuizawa  the reunion with ibuki  confronting manabe","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4-p97-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3: the holdout and the odd-moves list<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.97, p.108<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named as one of the last left in the Rabbit room after the first discussion breaks up.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The last people in the room are the three Class B students and Ibuki.<span class=\"pg\">p.97<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Appears in Ayanokōji’s list of things that had been off with Horikita since the test began: Karuizawa, the reunion with Ibuki, confronting Manabe.<span class=\"pg\">p.108<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4-p94-1\">← Before: Ch.3 sec. 3.1: the outsider’s verdict<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4-p127-1\">→ After: Ch.4: outer and inner<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4-p127-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"ibuki-mio","q":"ibuki mio ch 4  outer and inner named as an example of the gap between a person s outer and inner selves  innermost thoughts aren t immediately apparent   take kushida  ibuki  or even me","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4-p127-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4: outer and inner<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.127<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named as an example of the gap between a person’s outer and inner selves.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Innermost thoughts aren’t immediately apparent — take Kushida, Ibuki, or even me.<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4-p97-1\">← Before: Ch.3: the holdout and the odd-moves list<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4-p128-1\">→ After: Ch.4 sec. 4.0: not at the shade meeting<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4-p128-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"ryuuen-kakeru ibuki-mio","q":"ibuki mio ch 4 sec  4 0  not at the shade meeting named once as absent from ryuuen s side when he drops into the horikita conversation   he wasn t with ibuki  apparently    the usual pair is split for this scene  no dialogue and no further presence in the range","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4-p128-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4 sec. 4.0: not at the shade meeting<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.128<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named once as absent from Ryuuen’s side when he drops into the Horikita conversation.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> “He wasn’t with Ibuki, apparently” — the usual pair is split for this scene.<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> No dialogue and no further presence in the range.<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4-p127-1\">← Before: Ch.4: outer and inner<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4-p155-1\">→ After: Ch.4: apart from Ichinose<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4-p155-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"ibuki-mio","q":"ibuki mio ch 4  apart from ichinose named as one of the two class b girls not staring at machida  apart from ichinose and ibuki  the girls seemed interested in machida","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4-p155-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4: apart from Ichinose<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.155<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named as one of the two Class B girls not staring at Machida.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Apart from Ichinose and Ibuki, the girls seemed interested in Machida.<span class=\"pg\">p.155<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4-p128-1\">← Before: Ch.4 sec. 4.0: not at the shade meeting<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4-p159-1\">→ After: Ch.4 sec. 4.2: the absent buffer<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4-p159-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"karuizawa-kei manabe-shiho ibuki-mio","q":"ibuki mio ch 4 sec  4 2  the absent buffer named as the class c girl who might have mitigated the trio on karuizawa s tail   and she wasn t around  her absence is why the three can close on karuizawa alone in the corridor  the buffer between manabe s set and karuizawa is missing for the stairwell  no dialogue in this range  presence is the narrator s counterfactual","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4-p159-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4 sec. 4.2: the absent buffer<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.159<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named as the Class C girl who might have mitigated the trio on Karuizawa’s tail — and she wasn’t around.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"manabe-shiho.html\">Manabe Shiho<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Her absence is why the three can close on Karuizawa alone in the corridor.<span class=\"pg\">p.159<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Manabe Shiho<\/b> The buffer between Manabe’s set and Karuizawa is missing for the stairwell.<span class=\"pg\">p.159<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> No dialogue in this range; presence is the narrator’s counterfactual.<span class=\"pg\">p.159<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4-p155-1\">← Before: Ch.4: apart from Ichinose<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4-p222-1\">→ After: Ch.5 sec. 5.2: the lone girl agrees<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4-p222-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"manabe-shiho hamaguchi-tetsuya yukimura-teruhiko ibuki-mio","q":"ibuki mio ch 5 sec  5 2  the lone girl agrees the unexpected first volunteer after ayanokoji   threatens manabe into the show with the vip or class logic   anyone who isn t the vip or who s not in the same class as a vip gains nothing if things keep going like this  class b understands that  if we sit around  we won t catch up to the classes above us  that s why they re showing everyone their phones  i agree with their idea  she answered  enemy tone  not ally   or maybe you re the vip     in that case  show everyone your phone   or maybe you re the vip  said ibuki   in that case  show everyone your phone  backs his plan as class b s shared interest   the classes above only move if the lower ones show   a lone girl agreed  among the scoffers   the first volunteer after the swap phone   you know  you ve been really jumpy  you re not the vip  are you  ibuki asked    the jibe that freezes him   you know  you ve been really jumpy  you re not the vip  are you  ibuki asked","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4-p222-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.5 sec. 5.2: the lone girl agrees<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.222–223<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The unexpected first volunteer after Ayanokōji — threatens Manabe into the show with the VIP-or-class logic.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"manabe-shiho.html\">Manabe Shiho<\/a> · <a href=\"hamaguchi-tetsuya.html\">Hamaguchi Tetsuya<\/a> · <a href=\"yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Anyone who isn’t the VIP or who’s not in the same class as a VIP gains nothing if things keep going like this. Class B understands that. If we sit around, we won’t catch up to the classes above us. That’s why they’re showing…”<span class=\"pg\">p.222<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Or maybe you’re the VIP,” said Ibuki.<span class=\"pg\">p.222<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“In that case, show everyone your phone.”<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Anyone who isn’t the VIP or who’s not in the same class as a VIP gains nothing if things keep going like this. Class B understands that. If we sit around, we won’t catch up to the classes above us. That’s why they’re showing everyone their phones. I agree with their idea,” she answered.<span class=\"pg\">p.222<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Manabe Shiho<\/b> Enemy tone, not ally: “Or maybe you’re the VIP” → “In that case, show everyone your phone.”<span class=\"pg\">p.222-223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hamaguchi Tetsuya<\/b> Backs his plan as Class B’s shared interest — the classes above only move if the lower ones show.<span class=\"pg\">p.222<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> “a lone girl agreed” among the scoffers — the first volunteer after the swap phone.<span class=\"pg\">p.222<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> “You know, you’ve been really jumpy. You’re not the VIP, are you?” Ibuki asked. — the jibe that freezes him.<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You know, you’ve been really jumpy. You’re not the VIP, are you?” Ibuki asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4-p159-1\">← Before: Ch.4 sec. 4.2: the absent buffer<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4_5-p20-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune ryuuen-kakeru ayanokouji-kiyotaka ibuki-mio","q":"ibuki mio ch 2 sec  2 1  the couples only encounter turned away from the couples only line  she spots ayanokoji in the next queue  chases him down  and demands to know where horikita is   where s horikita  the page recaps the island  sent to infiltrate class d  she and horikita traded blows in a fistfight  the narration reads her as hostile since   i hate seeing his face  even when i have to  the ship pairing was atonement    that was because it was my fault that i didn t discover class d s leader  she answered quietly  she presses him for class d s leader and does not believe the shrug   it s not like you don t know   i absolutely despise the girls in my class    the narration ranks her even more antisocial than horikita  with the right opportunity the two might get along  the cat allergy simile for her own trap   i m like someone who loves cats  but has an allergy   i suppose  when you put it that way  you have a point  she muttered   wait  why the hell are you lecturing me  ibuki glared   you seem like the sort who ll turn out to be a mass murderer later in life   put simply  it s a type of fortune telling that tells you what times are unlucky for you   fortune telling isn t all about romance and such","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4_5-p20-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 sec. 2.1: the couples-only encounter<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.20–27<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Turned away from the couples-only line, she spots Ayanokōji in the next queue, chases him down, and demands to know where Horikita is.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Where’s Horikita?”<span class=\"pg\">p.20<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I hate seeing his face, even when I have to.”<span class=\"pg\">p.23<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I suppose, when you put it that way, you have a point,” she muttered.<span class=\"pg\">p.26<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> The page recaps the island: sent to infiltrate Class D, she and Horikita traded blows in a fistfight; the narration reads her as hostile since.<span class=\"pg\">p.21<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> The ship pairing was atonement — “That was because it was my fault that I didn’t discover Class D’s leader,” she answered quietly.<span class=\"pg\">p.23<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> She presses him for Class D’s leader and does not believe the shrug: “It’s not like you don’t know.”<span class=\"pg\">p.23<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> “I absolutely despise the girls in my class” — the narration ranks her even more antisocial than Horikita; with the right opportunity the two might get along.<span class=\"pg\">p.24<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The cat-allergy simile for her own trap: “I’m like someone who loves cats, but has an allergy.”<span class=\"pg\">p.24<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Wait, why the hell are you lecturing me?” Ibuki glared.<span class=\"pg\">p.26<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You seem like the sort who’ll turn out to be a mass murderer later in life.”<span class=\"pg\">p.26<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Put simply, it’s a type of fortune-telling that tells you what times are unlucky for you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.26<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Fortune-telling isn’t all about romance and such.”<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4_5-p28-1\">→ After: Ch.2 sec. 2.2–2.3: named in the list, then fate<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4_5-p28-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka ibuki-mio","q":"ibuki mio ch 2 sec  2 2 2 3  named in the list  then fate named in ayanokoji s list of the people he will not invite  she is back at the booth the next day   same place  exact same time  on the couples only rule the two agree   ibuki and i agreed on that  the second meeting turns from the booth to belief  he asks directly whether she believes in fortune telling  and she answers that the over skeptical get nothing out of it","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4_5-p28-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 sec. 2.2–2.3: named in the list, then fate<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.28–29<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named in Ayanokōji’s list of the people he will not invite, she is back at the booth the next day — same place, exact same time.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> On the couples-only rule the two agree: “Ibuki and I agreed on that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> The second meeting turns from the booth to belief: he asks directly whether she believes in fortune-telling, and she answers that the over-skeptical get nothing out of it.<span class=\"pg\">p.29<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4_5-p20-1\">← Before: Ch.2 sec. 2.1: the couples-only encounter<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4_5-p30-1\">→ After: Ch.2 sec. 2.3: agreeing to the pair<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4_5-p30-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka ibuki-mio","q":"ibuki mio ch 2 sec  2 3  agreeing to the pair she accepts the pairing for the reading itself  then flags the island grudge her classmates may still hold against ayanokoji   i would like to have my fortune read  after all   some students still hold a bit of a grudge toward me because of what happened on the island  calls him  surprisingly shameless  for shrugging the grudge off  sets the queue rule  no pointless chit chat    we re only together to have our fortunes read","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4_5-p30-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 sec. 2.3: agreeing to the pair<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.30–32<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">She accepts the pairing for the reading itself, then flags the island grudge her classmates may still hold against Ayanokōji.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“I would like to have my fortune read, after all.”<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Some students still hold a bit of a grudge toward me because of what happened on the island.”<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Calls him “surprisingly shameless” for shrugging the grudge off; sets the queue rule: no pointless chit-chat — “We’re only together to have our fortunes read.”<span class=\"pg\">p.31–32<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4_5-p28-1\">← Before: Ch.2 sec. 2.2–2.3: named in the list, then fate<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4_5-p33-1\">→ After: Ch.2 sec. 2.4: her reading<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4_5-p33-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka ibuki-mio","q":"ibuki mio ch 2 sec  2 4  her reading first into the tent  name  id card  and  do whatever you want  to the warning about unpleasant sights   ibuki  ibuki mio  she answered flatly   do whatever you want  ibuki replied   thank you very much  said ibuki    the predictions are ordinary and bright  and she listens with satisfaction  genuinely shocked by the fate tenchuusatsu pronouncement  and explains it to him as a life of constant misfortune  annoyed at being called the little girl","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4_5-p33-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 sec. 2.4: her reading<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.33–37<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">First into the tent: name, ID card, and “Do whatever you want” to the warning about unpleasant sights.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Ibuki. Ibuki Mio,” she answered flatly.<span class=\"pg\">p.34<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Do whatever you want,” Ibuki replied.<span class=\"pg\">p.34<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Thank you very much,” said Ibuki. — the predictions are ordinary and bright, and she listens with satisfaction.<span class=\"pg\">p.35<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Genuinely shocked by the fate tenchuusatsu pronouncement, and explains it to him as a life of constant misfortune; annoyed at being called the little girl.<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4_5-p30-1\">← Before: Ch.2 sec. 2.3: agreeing to the pair<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4_5-p38-1\">→ After: Ch.2 sec. 2.5: the detour and the elevator<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4_5-p38-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka ibuki-mio","q":"ibuki mio ch 2 sec  2 5  the detour and the elevator she agrees the fortune teller is famous and accurate  then chooses the detour with him   to see how accurate   the fortune teller said not to take any detours  ibuki said  phone dead from a battery she never watches   i don t have anyone to talk to  so i don t usually notice when my battery is about to die   you re such a useless man   rejected  she countered  vetoes the idea outright   as long as it s not horikita  in the heat  kicks a dent into the elevator wall  and her jump reaches the ceiling hatch   strength ayanokoji grants he could not match in combat   i ll kick it  works the button combinations with him  punches the wall when they fail  and lands the floor plus close press that moves the car   fortune telling is serious business","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4_5-p38-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 sec. 2.5: the detour and the elevator<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.38–47<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">She agrees the fortune-teller is famous and accurate, then chooses the detour with him — to see how accurate.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“The fortune-teller said not to take any detours,” Ibuki said.<span class=\"pg\">p.38<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“You’re such a useless man.”<span class=\"pg\">p.40<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Rejected,” she countered.<span class=\"pg\">p.41<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Phone dead from a battery she never watches: “I don’t have anyone to talk to, so I don’t usually notice when my battery is about to die.”<span class=\"pg\">p.40<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Vetoes the idea outright: “As long as it’s not Horikita.”<span class=\"pg\">p.41<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> In the heat: kicks a dent into the elevator wall, and her jump reaches the ceiling hatch — strength Ayanokōji grants he could not match in combat.<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ll kick it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.44<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Works the button combinations with him, punches the wall when they fail, and lands the floor-plus-close press that moves the car: “Fortune-telling is serious business.”<span class=\"pg\">p.46–47<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4_5-p33-1\">← Before: Ch.2 sec. 2.4: her reading<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4_5-p49-1\">→ After: Ch.3: passing mentions<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4_5-p49-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"","w":"ibuki-mio","q":"ibuki mio ch 3  passing mentions the chapter dates itself one week before ak and ibuki ended up stuck in the elevator   a back reference to chapter 2  the elevator entrapment is already history  this volume s earlier chapters covered it  ak groups her with horikita as  stubborn loners like horikita and ibuki  whose birthdays kushida would be unlikely to know","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4_5-p49-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3: passing mentions<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.49, 61<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The chapter dates itself one week before AK and Ibuki ended up stuck in the elevator — a back-reference to Chapter 2.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Backstory<\/span> The elevator entrapment is already history; this volume&#x27;s earlier chapters covered it.<span class=\"pg\">p.49<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> AK groups her with Horikita as “stubborn loners like Horikita and Ibuki” whose birthdays Kushida would be unlikely to know.<span class=\"pg\">p.61<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4_5-p38-1\">← Before: Ch.2 sec. 2.5: the detour and the elevator<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4_5-p63-1\">→ After: Ch.3: a passing mention<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4_5-p63-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"","w":"ibuki-mio","q":"ibuki mio ch 3  a passing mention ibuki is named in the birthday hunt discussion as one of the class s stubborn loners  a line groups her with horikita as people whose information is hard to obtain","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4_5-p63-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3: a passing mention<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.63<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Ibuki is named in the birthday-hunt discussion as one of the class&#x27;s stubborn loners.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> A line groups her with Horikita as people whose information is hard to obtain.<span class=\"pg\">p.63<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4_5-p49-1\">← Before: Ch.3: passing mentions<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v5-p13-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"","w":"horikita-suzune ibuki-mio","q":"ibuki mio ch 2  passing mention named in the alphabetical rabbit group roster karuizawa recites   third  between ichinose san and karuizawa san  her place in the roster is the exhibit for the zodiac vip rule","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v5-p13-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2: passing mention<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.13<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named in the alphabetical rabbit-group roster Karuizawa recites — third, between Ichinose-san and Karuizawa-san.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Her place in the roster is the exhibit for the zodiac VIP rule.<span class=\"pg\">p.13<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v5-p94-1\">→ After: Ch.6 sec. 6: the rivalry heat<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v5-p94-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"action spoken","w":"horikita-suzune ibuki-mio","q":"ibuki mio ch 6 sec  6  the rivalry heat ibuki draws the same 100 metre group as horikita   her most bitter rival   and burns to beat her  starts better than horikita  stays neck and neck  then loses by a narrow margin at the tape  hyperawareness of horikita costs her the win  had she not watched her  the result might have differed   ibuki was faster than i expected  said horikita  kicks the ground in frustration after the loss  determined never to lose to horikita  no matter the event   fire in her eyes from the line","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v5-p94-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 sec. 6: the rivalry heat<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.94–95<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Ibuki draws the same 100-metre group as Horikita — her most bitter rival — and burns to beat her.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Ibuki was faster than I expected,” said Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.95<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Starts better than Horikita, stays neck and neck, then loses by a narrow margin at the tape.<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Hyperawareness of Horikita costs her the win; had she not watched her, the result might have differed.<span class=\"pg\">p.94–95<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Kicks the ground in frustration after the loss.<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Determined never to lose to Horikita, no matter the event — fire in her eyes from the line.<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v5-p13-1\">← Before: Ch.2: passing mention<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v5-p120-1\">→ After: Ch.6 sec. 6: the order on Horikita<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v5-p120-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"action","w":"horikita-suzune ryuuen-kakeru ibuki-mio","q":"ibuki mio ch 6 sec  6  the order on horikita ibuki rides as a class b c jockey in the girls  cavalry and singles out horikita  issues an order and heads straight for horikita   first of the four horsemen to commit  personal rivalry continues off the track  she is out for blood against the same girl she lost to in the dash  her charge fits ryuuen s plan even if the text does not say she was ordered by name for this moment","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v5-p120-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 sec. 6: the order on Horikita<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.120<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Ibuki rides as a Class B/C jockey in the girls’ cavalry and singles out Horikita.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q action\">Issues an order and heads straight for Horikita — first of the four horsemen to commit.<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Personal rivalry continues off the track: she is out for blood against the same girl she lost to in the dash.<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Her charge fits Ryuuen’s plan even if the text does not say she was ordered by name for this moment.<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v5-p94-1\">← Before: Ch.6 sec. 6: the rivalry heat<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v5-p200-1\">→ After: Ch.9 sec. 9.3: voice on the trap recording<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v5-p200-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"spoken","w":"ryuuen-kakeru horikita-suzune ibuki-mio","q":"ibuki mio ch 9 sec  9 3  voice on the trap recording ibuki s voice appears on the email recording of ryuuen s class c strategy meeting   look  i m not discounting your strategy or whatever  but give me a chance to fight horikita  interrupts ryuuen on the tape  he then orders her obstacle course collision with horikita and the staged injury  asks to fight horikita before ryuuen s plan is spelled out","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v5-p200-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.9 sec. 9.3: voice on the trap recording<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.200<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Ibuki’s voice appears on the email recording of Ryuuen’s Class C strategy meeting.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Look, I’m not discounting your strategy or whatever, but give me a chance to fight Horikita.”<span class=\"pg\">p.200<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Interrupts Ryuuen on the tape; he then orders her obstacle-course collision with Horikita and the staged injury.<span class=\"pg\">p.200<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Asks to fight Horikita before Ryuuen’s plan is spelled out.<span class=\"pg\">p.200<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v5-p120-1\">← Before: Ch.6 sec. 6: the order on Horikita<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v6-p62-1","v":"y1v6","y":1,"o":7,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune ryuuen-kakeru nishino-takeko manabe-shiho ibuki-mio","q":"ibuki mio ch 4 sec  4  the only one who talks back standing near the window  arms crossed  posture defiant   she challenges ryuuen s class d theory   what are you trying to say  ryuuen   i don t have that luxury  besides  you re just trying to intimidate the entire class  i gain nothing from silence  right   like you  then   i mean  you also failed to crush horikita in the sports festival  or to get the private points you expected  you re the same as me  her sports festival challenge to horikita ended in narrow defeat   the failure ryuuen throws back  equates their failures  he threatens to bury her if she keeps interrupting the spy game   so  how do you explain the results  you never explain anything  you seriously expect to convince us that class d has some master strategist   leaks information   wait  are you serious   wait  what  you re not seriously going to accept that class c has a traitor  are you  watches the phone seizure  ibuki s later hand raise is the public stand against it  demands an explanation and is put off with later  then the for show phone logic and the x audio debate   will you explain what s going on here   so  one of the people you thought were innocent like nishino is a traitor after all   what are you doing here  is there really even a spy  inner doubt  the shadowy puppeteer may be a story to hide ryuuen s own failure  evidence never surfaces against suzune   wait a minute  even if we assume that you didn t just record that file yourself  there are still questions that you need to answer  we never discussed the details of getting horikita to kneel before you  this other person managed to anticipate everything  including the time you were meeting her  that s impossible   i can t understand that   if they re from the same class  shouldn t he have protected horikita from the start   i don t get it  so  x has been helping class c   but there wasn t any proof on anyone s phone   you didn t even look at them carefully   huh  but you said you d know the spy s identity if you looked at our phones   well  no  i wouldn t  that s why i thought that checking our phones was a waste of time  questions whether threatened spies can really be called wild  reacts with a short startled word when ryuuen calls the spies  position a wild time   if they re being threatened by someone they don t know  that hardly seems  wild  defiant  analytical  unwilling to kneel to intimidation  the only class c voice that repeatedly forces ryuuen to answer","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v6-p62-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4 sec. 4: the only one who talks back<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V6 · p.62–69<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Standing near the window, arms crossed, posture defiant — she challenges Ryuuen’s Class D theory.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"nishino-takeko.html\">Nishino Takeko<\/a> · <a href=\"manabe-shiho.html\">Manabe Shiho<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“What are you trying to say, Ryuuen?”<span class=\"pg\">p.62<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I don’t have that luxury. Besides, you’re just trying to intimidate the entire class. I gain nothing from silence, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.62<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Like you, then?”<span class=\"pg\">p.62<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>25 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I mean, you also failed to crush Horikita in the sports festival, or to get the private points you expected. You’re the same as me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.62<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Her sports-festival challenge to Horikita ended in narrow defeat — the failure Ryuuen throws back.<span class=\"pg\">p.62<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Equates their failures; he threatens to bury her if she keeps interrupting the spy game.<span class=\"pg\">p.62–63<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So, how do you explain the results? You never explain anything. You seriously expect to convince us that Class D has some master strategist?”<span class=\"pg\">p.62<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Leaks information?”<span class=\"pg\">p.63<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Wait, are you serious?”<span class=\"pg\">p.63<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Wait, what? You’re not seriously going to accept that Class C has a traitor, are you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.63<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nishino Takeko<\/b> Watches the phone seizure; Ibuki’s later hand-raise is the public stand against it.<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Demands an explanation and is put off with Later.; then the for-show phone logic and the X-audio debate.<span class=\"pg\">p.66–69<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Will you explain what’s going on here?”<span class=\"pg\">p.66<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So, one of the people you thought were innocent—like Nishino—is a traitor after all,”<span class=\"pg\">p.67<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What are you doing here? Is there really even a spy?”<span class=\"pg\">p.67<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Inner doubt: the shadowy puppeteer may be a story to hide Ryuuen’s own failure; evidence never surfaces against Suzune.<span class=\"pg\">p.67–68<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Wait a minute. Even if we assume that you didn’t just record that file yourself, there are still questions that you need to answer. We never discussed the details of getting Horikita to kneel before you. This other person managed to anticipate everything, including the time you were meeting her? That’s impossible,”<span class=\"pg\">p.67<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I can’t understand that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.68<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If they’re from the same class, shouldn’t he have protected Horikita from the start?”<span class=\"pg\">p.68<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t get it. So, X has been helping Class C?”<span class=\"pg\">p.69<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But there wasn’t any proof on anyone’s phone.”<span class=\"pg\">p.69<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You didn’t even look at them carefully.”<span class=\"pg\">p.69<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Huh? But you said you’d know the spy’s identity if you looked at our phones.”<span class=\"pg\">p.69<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, no, I wouldn’t. That’s why I thought that checking our phones was a waste of time.”<span class=\"pg\">p.69<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Manabe Shiho<\/b> Questions whether threatened spies can really be called wild.<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Reacts with a short startled word when Ryuuen calls the spies’ position a wild time.<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If they’re being threatened by someone they don’t know, that hardly seems ‘wild.’”<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Defiant, analytical, unwilling to kneel to intimidation; the only Class C voice that repeatedly forces Ryuuen to answer.<span class=\"pg\">p.62–72<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v6-p73-1\">→ After: Ch.4: a passing mention in the spy grilling<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v6-p73-1","v":"y1v6","y":1,"o":7,"k":"","w":"ibuki-mio","q":"ibuki mio ch 4  a passing mention in the spy grilling named in ryuuen s interrogation of manabe s circle after the cafe smash  present as ryuuen s lieutenant while the spies recount who saw the bullying","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v6-p73-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4: a passing mention in the spy grilling<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V6 · p.73<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named in Ryuuen’s interrogation of Manabe’s circle after the café smash.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Present as Ryuuen’s lieutenant while the spies recount who saw the bullying.<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v6-p62-1\">← Before: Ch.4 sec. 4: the only one who talks back<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v7-p22-1","v":"y1v7","y":1,"o":8,"k":"","w":"ryuuen-kakeru ayanokouji-kiyotaka ibuki-mio","q":"ibuki mio ch 2  island spy in the retelling named in ayanokoji s island account as one of the spies who infiltrated the other classes  radio to spy story told under horikita s official credit  the full spy network is not spelled out to the group  his island command structure in the retelling  speaker of the account  keeps other details back","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v7-p22-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2: island spy in the retelling<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V7 · p.22–23<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named in Ayanokōji’s island account as one of the spies who infiltrated the other classes.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Radio-to-spy story told under Horikita’s official credit; the full spy network is not spelled out to the group.<span class=\"pg\">p.22–23<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> His island command structure in the retelling.<span class=\"pg\">p.22–23<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Speaker of the account; keeps other details back.<span class=\"pg\">p.22<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v7-p103-1\">→ After: Ch.4: with the path pack<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v7-p103-1","v":"y1v7","y":1,"o":8,"k":"","w":"ryuuen-kakeru kouenji-rokusuke ibuki-mio","q":"ibuki mio ch 4  with the path pack on the tree lined path with the class c group  did not accompany the classroom visit  muscle for the path ambush  part of the wall in front of him","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v7-p103-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4: with the path pack<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V7 · p.103<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"kouenji-rokusuke.html\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> On the tree-lined path with the Class C group; did not accompany the classroom visit.<span class=\"pg\">p.103<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Muscle for the path ambush.<span class=\"pg\">p.103<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> Part of the wall in front of him.<span class=\"pg\">p.103<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v7-p22-1\">← Before: Ch.2: island spy in the retelling<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v7-p121-1\">→ After: Ch.5 sec. 5.1–5.2: the reluctant hand<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v7-p121-1","v":"y1v7","y":1,"o":8,"k":"spoken","w":"ryuuen-kakeru karuizawa-kei yamada-albert ishizaki-daichi ibuki-mio","q":"ibuki mio ch 5 sec  5 1 5 2  the reluctant hand named in ryuuen s head as the one who called identifying x meaningless  joins the rooftop party anyway   so  where are we going  cut the crap and tell us   you make me nervous  dragging me into all your stupid schemes   concerned  ibuki   but you sent a threatening message to karuizawa  right  what if she tattles to the school  if x puts the idea in her head  she might   no way  this is insane   it all depends on your plan  if i think it s dangerous  i ll leave   you painted over the camera   isn t that a punishable offense   aren t you getting carried away  ryuuen  she might still have something up her sleeve   ibuki  hold karuizawa down   why me  you can do it yourself  can t you   i won t be complicit in this  it s too risky   do it   look  i ve got problems of my own  sorry  clicks her tongue but approaches  moves behind karuizawa and grabs her hands with martial arts ease  curious about x yet openly disgusted by the method  stays because she wants the name  not the cruelty  follower who questions the plan and still executes it  the restraint on the roof  paired at the rooftop door  the other class c on the roof","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v7-p121-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.5 sec. 5.1–5.2: the reluctant hand<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V7 · p.121–134<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named in Ryuuen’s head as the one who called identifying X meaningless; joins the rooftop party anyway.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"yamada-albert.html\">Yamada Albert<\/a> · <a href=\"ishizaki-daichi.html\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“So, where are we going? Cut the crap and tell us”<span class=\"pg\">p.123<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“You make me nervous, dragging me into all your stupid schemes.”<span class=\"pg\">p.123<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> “Concerned, Ibuki?”<span class=\"pg\">p.123<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>17 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But…you sent a threatening message to Karuizawa, right? What if she tattles to the school? If X puts the idea in her head, she might.”<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No way. This is insane!”<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It all depends on your plan. If I think it’s dangerous, I’ll leave.”<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You painted over the camera?”<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Isn’t that a punishable offense?”<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Aren’t you getting carried away, Ryuuen? She might still have something up her sleeve,”<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ibuki, hold Karuizawa down.”<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Why me? You can do it yourself, can’t you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I won’t be complicit in this. It’s too risky,”<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Do it,”<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Look, I’ve got problems of my own. Sorry,”<span class=\"pg\">p.134<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Clicks her tongue but approaches; moves behind Karuizawa and grabs her hands with martial-arts ease.<span class=\"pg\">p.134<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Curious about X yet openly disgusted by the method; stays because she wants the name, not the cruelty.<span class=\"pg\">p.121–134<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Follower who questions the plan and still executes it.<span class=\"pg\">p.121–134<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> The restraint on the roof.<span class=\"pg\">p.133–134<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yamada Albert<\/b> Paired at the rooftop door.<span class=\"pg\">p.122, 125<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/b> The other Class C on the roof.<span class=\"pg\">p.122, 125<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v7-p103-1\">← Before: Ch.4: with the path pack<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v7-p136-1\">→ After: Ch.5 half2: the hand that stays<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v7-p136-1","v":"y1v7","y":1,"o":8,"k":"spoken","w":"ryuuen-kakeru karuizawa-kei ishizaki-daichi ibuki-mio","q":"ibuki mio ch 5 half2  the hand that stays shocked when ryuuen shows he knows karuizawa s history   how could you know that  ryuuen   and you think that person s x   how could you know that  ryuuen  fires questions about the two buckets and the prior research  admits she does not know the camera count   you said that there were two buckets  how did you know  did you investigate this all beforehand   huh  of course not  averts her eyes when the first bucket falls  she cannot watch   i can t watch this  i knew i shouldn t have helped you   i can t watch this   you re evil  this is disgusting   i ll leave after you get a name out of her  doesn t leave  leans against the door  ryuuen notes he isn t doing this to entertain her  disgust that never turns into departure  curiosity about x keeps her on the roof  the torturer she calls evil and still waits for  the girl she holds and watches break  fellow class c on the roof","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v7-p136-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.5 half2: the hand that stays<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V7 · p.136–141<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"ishizaki-daichi.html\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“And you think that person’s X?”<span class=\"pg\">p.136<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“How could you know that, Ryuuen?”<span class=\"pg\">p.136<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“You said that there were two buckets. How did you know? Did you investigate this all beforehand”?<span class=\"pg\">p.137<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>13 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Shocked when Ryuuen shows he knows Karuizawa’s history: “How could you know that, Ryuuen?”<span class=\"pg\">p.136<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Fires questions about the two buckets and the prior research; admits she does not know the camera count.<span class=\"pg\">p.137<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Huh? Of course not.”<span class=\"pg\">p.137<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Averts her eyes when the first bucket falls: she cannot watch.<span class=\"pg\">p.139<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I can’t watch this. I knew I shouldn’t have helped you,”<span class=\"pg\">p.139<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I can’t watch this,”<span class=\"pg\">p.140<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re evil. This is disgusting.”<span class=\"pg\">p.140<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ll leave after you get a name out of her,”<span class=\"pg\">p.140<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Doesn’t leave; leans against the door. Ryuuen notes he isn’t doing this to entertain her.<span class=\"pg\">p.140–141<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Disgust that never turns into departure; curiosity about X keeps her on the roof.<span class=\"pg\">p.136–141<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> The torturer she calls evil and still waits for.<span class=\"pg\">p.136–141<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> The girl she holds and watches break.<span class=\"pg\">p.136–141<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/b> Fellow Class C on the roof.<span class=\"pg\">p.136–137<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v7-p121-1\">← Before: Ch.5 sec. 5.1–5.2: the reluctant hand<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v7-p166-1\">→ After: Ch.6: the first to speak, the last to believe<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v7-p166-1","v":"y1v7","y":1,"o":8,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka ryuuen-kakeru ishizaki-daichi karuizawa-kei ibuki-mio","q":"ibuki mio ch 6  the first to speak  the last to believe first to notice ayanokoji on the roof  spends the half refusing to accept that he is x   ayano kouji   there s no way  it definitely can t be him   x is just using ayanokouji  don t be fooled  ryuuen  x probably told karuizawa in advance that he d send someone to come and save her   it s obviously a lie   you came here on someone else s orders  ayanokouji   it s not about what i want to believe  i m telling you  he can t be  he s  this guy s stupidly good natured  he s a softie  besides  he probably doesn t even know about karuizawa  and x  and everything don t you think   did that make you happy   quit joking around  of course it didn t make me happy  i was actually guilty of the crime  it just told me that he s an incompetent student who doesn t know how to doubt someone clearly suspicious   stop trying to make yourself look cool  you didn t even target ayanokouji or hirata until well after that  did you   but   hah  isn t that suspicious   would x really just come right out and say that   that s not true  we know your identity  we also know karuizawa s secret  awful things will happen tomorrow if you leave here without doing as we say  actually ryuuen s line attributed in dialogue flow   ibuki s own next line is below   that s enough  ryuuen  there s absolutely no way x would just stroll up here alone   h how did you know that   wait wait a second  yeah  he might be really clever  but that isn t enough to say for sure that he s x  right   it just doesn t make sense  if ayanokouji really is x  the mastermind  why would he just show up here  he wrecked all your plans so far  didn t he   all this time spent hyping up the mysterious  x  and he s nothing but talk  what a disappointment  maybe the digital camera thing was just dumb luck   so what  defends ayanokoji as too soft to be x using the island underwear sabotage   then is proven wrong by his own camera story  distrusts ryuuen enough to argue in front of him  needs proof before she flips  the man she keeps calling incompetent until the camera detail lands  the boss she contradicts on the roof  fellow class c who also doubts  the girl whose rescue plan she attributes to x","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v7-p166-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6: the first to speak, the last to believe<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V7 · p.166–174<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">First to notice Ayanokōji on the roof; spends the half refusing to accept that he is X.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"ishizaki-daichi.html\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/a> · <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Ayano…kouji?”<span class=\"pg\">p.166<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“There’s no way. It definitely can’t be him,”<span class=\"pg\">p.167<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“X is just using Ayanokouji. Don’t be fooled, Ryuuen. X probably told Karuizawa in advance that he’d send someone to come and save her!”<span class=\"pg\">p.167<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>23 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s obviously a lie,”<span class=\"pg\">p.167<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You came here on someone else’s orders, Ayanokouji.”<span class=\"pg\">p.167<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s not about what I want to believe. I’m telling you; he can’t be. He’s… This guy’s stupidly good-natured. He’s a softie. Besides, he probably doesn’t even know about Karuizawa, and X, and everything—don’t you think?”<span class=\"pg\">p.167<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Did that make you happy?”<span class=\"pg\">p.168<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Quit joking around. Of course it didn’t make me happy; I was actually guilty of the crime. It just told me that he’s an incompetent student who doesn’t know how to doubt someone clearly suspicious.”<span class=\"pg\">p.168<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Stop trying to make yourself look cool. You didn’t even target Ayanokouji or Hirata until well after that, did you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.170<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But—!”<span class=\"pg\">p.170<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Hah! Isn’t that suspicious?”<span class=\"pg\">p.170<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Would X really just come right out and say that?”<span class=\"pg\">p.170<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s not true. We know your identity. We also know Karuizawa’s secret. Awful things will happen tomorrow if you leave here without doing as we say,”<span class=\"pg\">p.171<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Actually Ryuuen’s line attributed in dialogue flow — Ibuki’s own next line is below.<span class=\"pg\">p.171<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s enough, Ryuuen. There’s absolutely no way X would just stroll up here alone,”<span class=\"pg\">p.171<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “H-how did you know that?!”<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Wait—wait a second. Yeah, he might be really clever, but that isn’t enough to say for sure that he’s X, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It just doesn’t make sense! If Ayanokouji really is X, the mastermind, why would he just show up here?! He wrecked all your plans so far, didn’t he?!”<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “All this time spent hyping up the mysterious ‘X,’ and he’s nothing but talk. What a disappointment. Maybe the digital-camera thing was just dumb luck,”<span class=\"pg\">p.174<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So what?”<span class=\"pg\">p.174<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Defends Ayanokōji as too soft to be X using the island underwear sabotage — then is proven wrong by his own camera story.<span class=\"pg\">p.167–172<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Distrusts Ryuuen enough to argue in front of him; needs proof before she flips.<span class=\"pg\">p.166–174<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> The man she keeps calling incompetent until the camera detail lands.<span class=\"pg\">p.166–174<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> The boss she contradicts on the roof.<span class=\"pg\">p.166–174<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/b> Fellow Class C who also doubts.<span class=\"pg\">p.167, 170–174<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> The girl whose rescue plan she attributes to X.<span class=\"pg\">p.167<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v7-p136-1\">← Before: Ch.5 half2: the hand that stays<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v7-p175-1\">→ After: Ch.6: the slap, the kick flurry, the points<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v7-p175-1","v":"y1v7","y":1,"o":8,"k":"spoken","w":"ryuuen-kakeru ayanokouji-kiyotaka ishizaki-daichi horikita-suzune katsuragi-kouhei sakayanagi-arisu ibuki-mio","q":"ibuki mio ch 6  the slap  the kick flurry  the points agrees with ishizaki that the reveal is enough   then  when ryuuen chooses violence anyway  objects and is struck across the face   i agree  ayanokouji might actually sacrifice her   what you re about to do puts class c at risk   i cooperated with you because i thought you were acting for the class s sake  but this is a step too far  ayanokouji clearly has nothing up his sleeve   iwon t be a part of what you re about to do   yes  because i ve watched you since april  you re going to hurt him  aren t you   ishizaki  komiya  kondou  even albert  you beat every single one of them until they were ready to obey you at all times   i m telling you  that kind of thinking is going to endanger our class  last line before ryuuen s slap  she falls silent   no way  y you re not messing around  are you  albert  ishizaki   s so  you re saying that ayanokouji turned the tables on you   hmm  tilts her head in confusion at the long explanation   seriously  what s the deal with you two   seriously  what are you   you honestly make me mad  i m not sure why  but you piss me off  kicks at ayanokoji in fury  he ends it with a neck throw   what  glares at both fighters when ryuuen slides the phone to her feet   huh  ryuuen  what are you saying  are you nuts   stop screwing around  why would you entrust your points to me   are are you really okay with that  asked of ryuuen as he prepares to leave  bests a healthy horikita on the island in the page s own comparison  still cannot touch ayanokoji  the only class c who tries to stop the violence  is slapped for it  then inherits the tyrant s points against her will  the boss who slaps her and then empties his account into her hands  the man she cannot believe  then cannot hit  fellow class c who wants the fight to end  the island fight used as her measuring stick  named in the contract void warning  same","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v7-p175-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6: the slap, the kick flurry, the points<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V7 · p.175–176, 180–182, 193–195<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Agrees with Ishizaki that the reveal is enough — then, when Ryuuen chooses violence anyway, objects and is struck across the face.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"ishizaki-daichi.html\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a> · <a href=\"sakayanagi-arisu.html\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“I agree. Ayanokouji might actually sacrifice her,”<span class=\"pg\">p.175<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“What you’re about to do puts Class C at risk,”<span class=\"pg\">p.176<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I cooperated with you because I thought you were acting for the class’s sake. But this is a step too far. Ayanokouji clearly has nothing up his sleeve.”<span class=\"pg\">p.176<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>27 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Iwon’t be a part of what you’re about to do.”<span class=\"pg\">p.176<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yes, because I’ve watched you since April. You’re going to hurt him, aren’t you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.176<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ishizaki. Komiya. Kondou. Even Albert. You beat every single one of them until they were ready to obey you at all times,”<span class=\"pg\">p.176<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m telling you, that kind of thinking is going to endanger our class!”<span class=\"pg\">p.176<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Last line before Ryuuen’s slap; she falls silent.<span class=\"pg\">p.176<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No way. Y-you’re not messing around, are you? Albert? Ishizaki?”<span class=\"pg\">p.180<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “S-so, you’re saying that Ayanokouji turned the tables on you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.181<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Hmm?”<span class=\"pg\">p.181<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Tilts her head in confusion at the long explanation.<span class=\"pg\">p.181<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Seriously, what’s the deal with you two?!”<span class=\"pg\">p.182<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Seriously, what are you…?”<span class=\"pg\">p.182<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You honestly make me mad. I’m not sure why, but you piss me off!”<span class=\"pg\">p.182<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Kicks at Ayanokōji in fury; he ends it with a neck throw.<span class=\"pg\">p.182<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What?”<span class=\"pg\">p.193<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Glares at both fighters when Ryuuen slides the phone to her feet.<span class=\"pg\">p.193<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Huh? Ryuuen, what are you saying? Are you nuts?”<span class=\"pg\">p.194<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Stop screwing around! Why would you entrust your points to me?!”<span class=\"pg\">p.194<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Are…are you really okay with that?”<span class=\"pg\">p.194<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Asked of Ryuuen as he prepares to leave.<span class=\"pg\">p.195<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Bests a healthy Horikita on the island in the page’s own comparison; still cannot touch Ayanokōji.<span class=\"pg\">p.182<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The only Class C who tries to stop the violence, is slapped for it, then inherits the tyrant’s points against her will.<span class=\"pg\">p.175–195<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> The boss who slaps her and then empties his account into her hands.<span class=\"pg\">p.175–195<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> The man she cannot believe, then cannot hit.<span class=\"pg\">p.180–182<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/b> Fellow Class C who wants the fight to end.<span class=\"pg\">p.175, 193–194<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> The island fight used as her measuring stick.<span class=\"pg\">p.182<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> Named in the contract-void warning.<span class=\"pg\">p.194<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> Same.<span class=\"pg\">p.194<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v7-p166-1\">← Before: Ch.6: the first to speak, the last to believe<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v7-p198-1\">→ After: Ch.7: the eight-hundred-million checkmate<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v7-p198-1","v":"y1v7","y":1,"o":8,"k":"spoken","w":"ryuuen-kakeru ishizaki-daichi yamada-albert ayanokouji-kiyotaka ibuki-mio","q":"ibuki mio ch 7  the eight hundred million checkmate returns ryuuen s phone on the path  red nosed from waiting  then refuses to accept his quit   i don t exactly want to touch you  you foisted your phone on me  remember  i m just giving it back   who knows   are you really going to quit   do you remember what you said back when you fought ishizaki and albert  you said that the strongest person is whoever wins in the end  no matter how many times they lost before  that s exactly how it went when you fought them   are you really going to end this after losing to ayanokouji one time   what  that s super lame   don t give me  maybe   i cooperated with you because you said you d get us to class a  now you re just going to leave us in the lurch   i tolerated your tyranny  i put up with it because we had the same ultimate goal  even when class c got our points docked the other day  and you wouldn t tell us why  no one complained  we all believed you d get us to class a someday  and now you re just going to drop out  that s lame  so  lame   is there anything more pathetic   eight hundred million private points   after you tossed your phone over to me yesterday  i agonized about whether i should transfer your points to my account  but then i decided to have a look at what else was on your phone   if you were trying to make it to class a alone  two million points would ve been enough  so why come up with a strategy that includes this number  eight hundred million is the number of points necessary to get all of class c up to class a  isn t it  though i can t imagine how we d ever save up that many points   that s not what i m talking about   if you re going to drop out  then fight me   ah  that felt great  well  if you re going to quit  hurry up and do it  hits him down onto the pavement  then heads back to the dorms  named as one of the four in the rooftop fight  would be punished if the school learned the full story  reads ryuuen s private phone and finds the 800 000 000 point plan for all of class c   proof the tyrant s  alone  speech was a lie  waits in the cold  argues with facts not tears  then hits him when words fail  the boss who tried to quit  she keeps him honest with a phone screen  named in the fight memory and the teacher s list  same  the one loss she throws in his face","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v7-p198-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.7: the eight-hundred-million checkmate<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V7 · p.198–203<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Returns Ryuuen’s phone on the path, red-nosed from waiting, then refuses to accept his quit.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"ishizaki-daichi.html\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/a> · <a href=\"yamada-albert.html\">Yamada Albert<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“I don’t exactly want to touch you. You foisted your phone on me, remember? I’m just giving it back,”<span class=\"pg\">p.198<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Who knows?”<span class=\"pg\">p.198<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Are you really going to quit?”<span class=\"pg\">p.198<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>21 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Do you remember what you said back when you fought Ishizaki and Albert? You said that the strongest person is whoever wins in the end, no matter how many times they lost before. That’s exactly how it went when you fought them.”<span class=\"pg\">p.198<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Are you really going to end this after losing to Ayanokouji one time?”<span class=\"pg\">p.198<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What? That’s super lame.”<span class=\"pg\">p.198<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Don’t give me ‘maybe,’”<span class=\"pg\">p.198<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I cooperated with you because you said you’d get us to Class A. Now you’re just going to leave us in the lurch?”<span class=\"pg\">p.198<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I tolerated your tyranny. I put up with it because we had the same ultimate goal. Even when Class C got our points docked the other day, and you wouldn’t tell us why, no one complained. We all believed you’d get us to Class A someday. And now you’re just going to drop out? That’s lame. So, lame.”<span class=\"pg\">p.199<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Is there anything more pathetic?”<span class=\"pg\">p.199<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Eight hundred million private points,”<span class=\"pg\">p.199<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “After you tossed your phone over to me yesterday, I agonized about whether I should transfer your points to my account. But then I decided to have a look at what else was on your phone.”<span class=\"pg\">p.199<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If you were trying to make it to Class A alone, two million points would’ve been enough. So why come up with a strategy that includes this number? Eight hundred million is the number of points necessary to get all of Class C up to Class A, isn’t it? Though I can’t imagine how we’d ever save up that many points…”<span class=\"pg\">p.199<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s not what I’m talking about.”<span class=\"pg\">p.200<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If you’re going to drop out, then fight me,”<span class=\"pg\">p.200<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ah. That felt great. Well, if you’re going to quit, hurry up and do it,”<span class=\"pg\">p.200<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Hits him down onto the pavement, then heads back to the dorms.<span class=\"pg\">p.200<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Named as one of the four in the rooftop fight; would be punished if the school learned the full story.<span class=\"pg\">p.201, 203<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Reads Ryuuen’s private phone and finds the 800,000,000-point plan for all of Class C — proof the tyrant’s “alone” speech was a lie.<span class=\"pg\">p.199<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Waits in the cold, argues with facts not tears, then hits him when words fail.<span class=\"pg\">p.198–200<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> The boss who tried to quit; she keeps him honest with a phone screen.<span class=\"pg\">p.198–200<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/b> Named in the fight memory and the teacher’s list.<span class=\"pg\">p.198, 202<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yamada Albert<\/b> Same.<span class=\"pg\">p.198, 202<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> The one-loss she throws in his face.<span class=\"pg\">p.198<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v7-p175-1\">← Before: Ch.6: the slap, the kick flurry, the points<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v7_5-p45-1","v":"y1v7.5","y":1,"o":9,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka ryuuen-kakeru ishizaki-daichi manabe-shiho ibuki-mio","q":"ibuki mio ch 3  movie  warehouse  and the eight hundred million question christmas eve ish afternoon movie  ibuki sits alone beside ayanokoji  equipment fails  they end up trapped in a keyaki mall warehouse and fight   geh  she gave a disgusted grunt   armrest collision   sound only  kept as printed   jeez  i really have no luck at all   all this time  you ve made fun of me  i can t forgive you for that   i hate you  i hate your lying  two faced bullshit  you show the world a fake personality and keep the real you locked away   if you want me to back down  have another match with me   i didn t think you d go easy on me just because i m female  but you really were merciless   you re the strongest person i ve ever seen  stronger than any adult  how d you get that strong   you know that a student needs twenty million points to get to class a  right  for an entire class to do so  they need a combined total of eight hundred million points  do you think it s even possible to save such an absurd number  rooftop grudge  forced rematch  concedes defeat  severs ties but expects to face him again  hates ryuuen s guts but hates more that ayanokoji took him down  still respects ryuuen s abilities through ishizaki  overhears his class c cover story with komiya and kondou  named in ayanokoji s list of people who could be caught if the roof story spread  goal  see every movie they screen at the school   simple on paper  hard to sustain  martial arts kicks in a cramped warehouse  tapped out after a throat grab  not knocked out","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v7_5-p45-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3: movie, warehouse, and the eight-hundred-million question<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V7.5 · p.45–64<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Christmas Eve-ish afternoon movie; Ibuki sits alone beside Ayanokōji; equipment fails; they end up trapped in a Keyaki Mall warehouse and fight.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"ishizaki-daichi.html\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/a> · <a href=\"manabe-shiho.html\">Manabe Shiho<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Geh!” She gave a disgusted grunt. (armrest collision — sound only; kept as printed)<span class=\"pg\">p.48<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Jeez. I really have no luck at all.”<span class=\"pg\">p.48<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“All this time, you’ve made fun of me. I can’t forgive you for that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.48<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>11 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I hate you. I hate your lying, two-faced bullshit. You show the world a fake personality and keep the real you locked away.”<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If you want me to back down, have another match with me,”<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I didn’t think you’d go easy on me just because I’m female, but you really were merciless.”<span class=\"pg\">p.62<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re the strongest person I’ve ever seen. Stronger than any adult. How’d you get that strong?”<span class=\"pg\">p.63<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You know that a student needs twenty million points to get to Class A, right? For an entire class to do so, they need a combined total of eight hundred million points. Do you think it’s even possible to save such an absurd number?”<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Rooftop grudge; forced rematch; concedes defeat; severs ties but expects to face him again.<span class=\"pg\">p.45–64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Hates Ryuuen’s guts but hates more that Ayanokōji took him down; still respects Ryuuen’s abilities through Ishizaki.<span class=\"pg\">p.49, 55<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/b> Overhears his Class C cover story with Komiya and Kondou.<span class=\"pg\">p.54–55<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Manabe Shiho<\/b> Named in Ayanokōji’s list of people who could be caught if the roof story spread.<span class=\"pg\">p.52<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Goal: see every movie they screen at the school — simple on paper, hard to sustain.<span class=\"pg\">p.53<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Martial-arts kicks in a cramped warehouse; tapped out after a throat grab, not knocked out.<span class=\"pg\">p.61–62<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v7_5-p76-1\">→ After: Ch.4: named in the bench talk<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v7_5-p76-1","v":"y1v7.5","y":1,"o":9,"k":"","w":"ryuuen-kakeru ayanokouji-kiyotaka ibuki-mio","q":"ibuki mio ch 4  named in the bench talk name hit in ayanokoji s explanation of why ryuuen surrendered   ibuki s presence on the roof  passing mention  ibuki  ishizaki  and albert had been there  their shared blame knowledge hastened the surrender  passing mention only  passing mention   ibuki spilled the beans  huh    ryuuen  ayanokoji says she only asked whether eight hundred million was possible  passing mention only  passing mention  ishizaki and ibuki  in particular  disliked ayanokoji and might push class c to challenge class d  passing mention only  present on the roof  asked the eight hundred million question that exposed the class wide point plan  the outsider who took ryuuen down  still disliked by her","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v7_5-p76-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4: named in the bench talk<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V7.5 · p.76, 80, 84<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Name-hit in Ayanokōji’s explanation of why Ryuuen surrendered — Ibuki’s presence on the roof.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Passing mention: Ibuki, Ishizaki, and Albert had been there; their shared-blame knowledge hastened the surrender.<span class=\"pg\">p.76<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> Passing mention only.<span class=\"pg\">p.76<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Passing mention: “Ibuki spilled the beans, huh?” — Ryuuen; Ayanokōji says she only asked whether eight hundred million was possible.<span class=\"pg\">p.80<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> Passing mention only.<span class=\"pg\">p.80<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Passing mention: Ishizaki and Ibuki, in particular, disliked Ayanokōji and might push Class C to challenge Class D.<span class=\"pg\">p.84<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> Passing mention only.<span class=\"pg\">p.84<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Present on the roof; asked the eight-hundred-million question that exposed the class-wide point plan.<span class=\"pg\">p.76, 80<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> The outsider who took Ryuuen down; still disliked by her.<span class=\"pg\">p.80, 84<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v7_5-p45-1\">← Before: Ch.3: movie, warehouse, and the eight-hundred-million question<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v7_5-p129-1\">→ After: Ch.5: not at this movie<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v7_5-p129-1","v":"y1v7.5","y":1,"o":9,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka ibuki-mio","q":"ibuki mio ch 5  not at this movie absence note while ayanokoji scans the fuller theater  passing mention   i didn t see ibuki  maybe she wasn t interested in an american animated film  or maybe she was just avoiding the crowds  passing mention only  the previous mall movie is why he checks for her  she is not here","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v7_5-p129-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.5: not at this movie<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V7.5 · p.129<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Absence note while Ayanokōji scans the fuller theater.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Passing mention: “I didn’t see Ibuki. Maybe she wasn’t interested in an American animated film, or maybe she was just avoiding the crowds.”<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> Passing mention only.<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> The previous mall movie is why he checks for her; she is not here.<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v7_5-p76-1\">← Before: Ch.4: named in the bench talk<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v8-p143-1","v":"y1v8","y":1,"o":10,"k":"","w":"horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka ibuki-mio","q":"ibuki mio ch 4  named as the island blind spot precedent not on the page  named when ayanokoji lists school rule blind spots from past exams  passing mention   such as how ibuki and horikita had traded blows back on the uninhabited island  even though violence was prohibited  passing mention only  the paired example of rule breaking that still did not sink the exam   violence prohibited  blows traded  part of his theory that every special exam has loopholes the school cannot fully close","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v8-p143-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4: named as the island blind-spot precedent<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V8 · p.143<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Not on the page; named when Ayanokōji lists school-rule blind spots from past exams.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Passing mention: “Such as how Ibuki and Horikita had traded blows back on the uninhabited island, even though violence was prohibited.”<span class=\"pg\">p.143<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> Passing mention only.<span class=\"pg\">p.143<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> The paired example of rule-breaking that still did not sink the exam — violence prohibited, blows traded.<span class=\"pg\">p.143<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Part of his theory that every special exam has loopholes the school cannot fully close.<span class=\"pg\">p.143<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v9-p56-1","v":"y1v9","y":1,"o":11,"k":"","w":"ryuuen-kakeru ibuki-mio","q":"ibuki mio camp group in ayanokoji s elimination list named with ryuuen  ishizaki and albert as the training camp group  does not appear  only in the internal list","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v9-p56-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Camp group in Ayanokōji’s elimination list<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V9 · p.56<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Named with Ryuuen, Ishizaki and Albert as the training-camp group.<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Does not appear; only in the internal list.<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v9-p153-1\">→ After: The rumor victim in the fight<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v9-p153-1","v":"y1v9","y":1,"o":11,"k":"action spoken","w":"ibuki-mio","q":"ibuki mio the rumor victim in the fight came with the class d group  one of the students the forum rumors targeted   telling me to stop after picking the fight yourself  well aren t you full of it  like ishizaki  she had fallen victim to the rumors posted on the school s forums  her kick speed and strength surprise hashimoto  her dropped phone and student id card start the id card thread  kicks at miyake s head  then knocks kito s lunge away the moment ishizaki warns her","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v9-p153-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The rumor victim in the fight<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V9 · p.153–161<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Came with the Class D group; one of the students the forum rumors targeted.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Telling me to stop after picking the fight yourself, well aren’t you full of it?”<span class=\"pg\">p.158<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Fact<\/span> Like Ishizaki, she had fallen victim to the rumors posted on the school’s forums.<span class=\"pg\">p.158<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Her kick speed and strength surprise Hashimoto; her dropped phone and student ID card start the ID-card thread.<span class=\"pg\">p.160<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Kicks at Miyake’s head, then knocks Kitō’s lunge away the moment Ishizaki warns her.<span class=\"pg\">p.161<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v9-p56-1\">← Before: Camp group in Ayanokōji’s elimination list<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v10-p240-1","v":"y1v10","y":1,"o":12,"k":"spoken","w":"manabe-shiho ishizaki-daichi ryuuen-kakeru ibuki-mio","q":"ibuki mio ch 6  seeing ryuen off and recovering points watches ryuen leave the classroom after school  manabe provokes her about being less important   well well  that s quite the miserable look on your face  now isn t it  are you really  that  sad to see ryuuen get expelled  goes with ishizaki to talk about ryuen s private points   come with me for a bit  ibuki  decides to recover ryuen s private points and meet him that night   i m going to see ryuen tonight and recover the private points  i might be the only one who can  visits ryuen s dorm room  he answers in boxers after a bath  demands his private points and receives them transferred to her phone   your private points  hand them over  is grabbed by ryuen  kicked toward the wall  then released after a warning about suzune   are you satisfied with your time here  at this school  leaves ryuen s room with his points and calls someone to report she has them  visits him  recovers his private points  and receives a warning  goes with him to talk and agrees to recover the points  provoked by her after ryuen leaves","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v10-p240-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6: Seeing Ryūen off and recovering points<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V10 · p.240–251<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Watches Ryūen leave the classroom after school; Manabe provokes her about being less important. Goes with Ishizaki to talk about Ryūen’s private points. Decides to recover Ryūen’s private points and meet him that night. Visits Ryūen’s dorm room; he answers in boxers after a bath. Demands his private points and receives them transferred to her phone. Is grabbed by Ryūen, kicked toward the wall, then released after a warning about Suzune. Leaves Ryūen’s room with his points and calls someone to report she has them.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"manabe-shiho.html\">Manabe Shiho<\/a> · <a href=\"ishizaki-daichi.html\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/a> · <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Manabe Shiho<\/b> “Well well, that’s quite the miserable look on your face, now isn’t it? Are you really ‘that’ sad to see Ryuuen get expelled?”<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/b> “Come with me for a bit, Ibuki.”<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I’m going to see Ryūen tonight and recover the private points. I might be the only one who can.”<span class=\"pg\">p.246<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Your private points. Hand them over.”<span class=\"pg\">p.248<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Are you satisfied with your time here, at this school?”<span class=\"pg\">p.250<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Visits him, recovers his private points, and receives a warning.<span class=\"pg\">p.247–251<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/b> Goes with him to talk and agrees to recover the points.<span class=\"pg\">p.242, 246<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Manabe Shiho<\/b> Provoked by her after Ryūen leaves.<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v10-p245-1\">→ After: Ch.6/Epilogue: Added voice lines<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v10-p245-1","v":"y1v10","y":1,"o":12,"k":"spoken","w":"ishizaki-daichi ichinose-honami ibuki-mio","q":"ibuki mio ch 6 epilogue  added voice lines asks ishizaki whether he really wants ryuen expelled   you don t really want ryuen to be expelled  do you  reports by phone that she has recovered all of ryuen s private points   it s me  i ve gotten all of ryuen s private points  tells ayanokoji she wants manabe expelled   manabe  it s just my personal preference though  calls ichinose an idiot for throwing away her points   you re an idiot  aren t you ichinose  discusses saving ryuen with him  makes the deal to save ryuen with her","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v10-p245-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6/Epilogue: Added voice lines<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V10 · p.245, 334, 338, 344<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Asks Ishizaki whether he really wants Ryūen expelled. Reports by phone that she has recovered all of Ryūen’s private points. Tells Ayanokōji she wants Manabe expelled. Calls Ichinose an idiot for throwing away her points.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ishizaki-daichi.html\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/a> · <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“You don’t really want Ryūen to be expelled, do you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.245<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“It’s me. I’ve gotten all of Ryūen’s private points.”<span class=\"pg\">p.334<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Manabe. It’s just my personal preference though.”<span class=\"pg\">p.338<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re an idiot, aren’t you Ichinose?”<span class=\"pg\">p.344<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/b> Discusses saving Ryūen with him.<span class=\"pg\">p.245<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Makes the deal to save Ryūen with her.<span class=\"pg\">p.338, 344<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v10-p240-1\">← Before: Ch.6: Seeing Ryūen off and recovering points<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v10-p245-2\">→ After: Ch.6: Recalling Ayanokōji’s words<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v10-p245-2","v":"y1v10","y":1,"o":12,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka ibuki-mio","q":"ibuki mio ch 6  recalling ayanokoji s words ibuki recalls ayanokoji s warning about the exam   this exam isn t simple enough for you to be able to save someone just because you say you want to  remembers his words while deciding whether to act","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v10-p245-2\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6: Recalling Ayanokōji’s words<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V10 · p.245<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Ibuki recalls Ayanokōji’s warning about the exam.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “This exam isn’t simple enough for you to be able to save someone just because you say you want to.”<span class=\"pg\">p.245<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Remembers his words while deciding whether to act.<span class=\"pg\">p.245<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v10-p245-1\">← Before: Ch.6/Epilogue: Added voice lines<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v10-p319-1\">→ After: Epilogue: Saving Ryūen (flashback)<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v10-p319-1","v":"y1v10","y":1,"o":12,"k":"spoken","w":"ryuuen-kakeru ishizaki-daichi ichinose-honami ayanokouji-kiyotaka manabe-shiho ibuki-mio","q":"ibuki mio epilogue  saving ryuen  flashback  visits ayanokoji s room with ishizaki at night to ask how to prevent ryuen s expulsion  says she was forced to come along and that ayanokoji would not cooperate  admits she does not want to beg ryuen for his points but later recovers them  calls ayanokoji to report she has obtained all of ryuen s private points and comes to his room with ishizaki  chooses manabe shiho as the replacement target to be expelled instead of ryuen  agrees with ichinose to exchange ryuen s points for class b s 40 praise votes to save him   it  it just pisses me off that he s running away before i can pay him back for this stupid loan i took from him  that s all there is to it  helps save him from expulsion by using his points  works with him to seek help and carry out the plan  negotiates with her to secure praise votes for ryuen  asks for his help and follows his plan  chooses her as the replacement target","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v10-p319-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Epilogue: Saving Ryūen (flashback)<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V10 · p.319–346<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Visits Ayanokōji’s room with Ishizaki at night to ask how to prevent Ryūen’s expulsion. Says she was forced to come along and that Ayanokōji would not cooperate. Admits she does not want to beg Ryūen for his points but later recovers them. Calls Ayanokōji to report she has obtained all of Ryūen’s private points and comes to his room with Ishizaki. Chooses Manabe Shiho as the replacement target to be expelled instead of Ryūen. Agrees with Ichinose to exchange Ryūen’s points for Class B’s 40 praise votes to save him.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"ishizaki-daichi.html\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/a> · <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"manabe-shiho.html\">Manabe Shiho<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“It… It just pisses me off that he’s running away before I can pay him back for this stupid loan I took from him, that’s all there is to it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.345<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Helps save him from expulsion by using his points.<span class=\"pg\">p.319–346<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/b> Works with him to seek help and carry out the plan.<span class=\"pg\">p.319–346<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Negotiates with her to secure praise votes for Ryūen.<span class=\"pg\">p.342–346<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Asks for his help and follows his plan.<span class=\"pg\">p.319–346<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Manabe Shiho<\/b> Chooses her as the replacement target.<span class=\"pg\">p.338–339<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v10-p245-2\">← Before: Ch.6: Recalling Ayanokōji’s words<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v11-p149-1","v":"y1v11","y":1,"o":13,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka ryuuen-kakeru ishizaki-daichi ibuki-mio","q":"ibuki mio year 1  vol  11 5 ch 3   depth review  the hostile walk to the mall bumps into ayanokoji in the dorm elevator  then ends up walking beside him toward keyaki mall   you again   you say that  but i don t want to have anything to do with you anymore   it s not going to break down again   shut up  you re noisy   you know why you got kicked  i m not going to say anything else  so get away from me   stupid idiot   impossible  impossible  absolutely impossible   he definitely won t help   you re weird  why are you happy about going up against him again  openly hostile toward ayanokoji yet won t be the first to break away   stubborn  unable to accept defeat  walks with him in tense silence  remains dismissive but now able to hold a conversation  went along with the covert gathering for his sake  showing she regards him as integral to the class  kicks him for teasing her and dismisses his recruitment plan as impossible","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v11-p149-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Year 1, Vol. 11.5 Ch.3 — Depth review: the hostile walk to the mall<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V11 · <\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Bumps into Ayanokōji in the dorm elevator, then ends up walking beside him toward Keyaki Mall.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"ishizaki-daichi.html\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;You again…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.149<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;You say that… but I don&#x27;t want to have anything to do with you anymore.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.150<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;It&#x27;s not going to break down again…?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.150<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>10 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Shut up, you&#x27;re noisy.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You know why you got kicked. I&#x27;m not going to say anything else, so get away from me.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Stupid-idiot.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Impossible, impossible, absolutely impossible.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.154<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;He definitely won&#x27;t help.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.156<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You&#x27;re weird. Why are you happy about going up against him again?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.157<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Openly hostile toward Ayanokōji yet won&#x27;t be the first to break away — stubborn, unable to accept defeat.<span class=\"pg\">p.150–152<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Walks with him in tense silence; remains dismissive but now able to hold a conversation.<span class=\"pg\">p.149–157<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Went along with the covert gathering for his sake, showing she regards him as integral to the class.<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/b> Kicks him for teasing her and dismisses his recruitment plan as impossible.<span class=\"pg\">p.152–156<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v11-p383-1\">→ After: Ch.8: Planning against Class B<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v11-p383-1","v":"y1v11","y":1,"o":13,"k":"","w":"ishizaki-daichi shiina-hiyori ryuuen-kakeru ibuki-mio","q":"ibuki mio ch 8  planning against class b meets with ishizaki and shiina in a karaoke room to discuss the special exam  is surprised to learn shiina invited ryuen and tries to leave when he is late  confronts ryuen when he finally arrives and demands he explain himself  questions the practicality of class d s event strategy but agrees to cooperate after hearing ryuen s plan  meets and argues with him while planning  is persuaded by her to stay and wait for ryuen  confronts him and ultimately agrees to follow his plan against class b","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v11-p383-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.8: Planning against Class B<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V11 · p.383–399<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Meets with Ishizaki and Shiina in a karaoke room to discuss the special exam. Is surprised to learn Shiina invited Ryūen and tries to leave when he is late. Confronts Ryūen when he finally arrives and demands he explain himself. Questions the practicality of Class D’s event strategy but agrees to cooperate after hearing Ryūen’s plan.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ishizaki-daichi.html\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/a> · <a href=\"shiina-hiyori.html\">Shiina Hiyori<\/a> · <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/b> Meets and argues with him while planning.<span class=\"pg\">p.383–399<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shiina Hiyori<\/b> Is persuaded by her to stay and wait for Ryūen.<span class=\"pg\">p.383–399<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Confronts him and ultimately agrees to follow his plan against Class B.<span class=\"pg\">p.387–399<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v11-p149-1\">← Before: Year 1, Vol. 11.5 Ch.3 — Depth review: the hostile walk to the mall<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v11-p385-1\">→ After: Ch.8: Waiting for Ryūen<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v11-p385-1","v":"y1v11","y":1,"o":13,"k":"spoken","w":"ishizaki-daichi shiina-hiyori ryuuen-kakeru ibuki-mio","q":"ibuki mio ch 8  waiting for ryuen says she does not have time for this   i don t have the time for this  says she is having fun with ishizaki and shiina   besides  i m having tons of fun spending time with you two  won t you stay  says she is at her limit   i can t take it anymore  i m at my limit  threatens to kick ryuen s ass   i ll kick your ass if you leave me here in karaoke hell any longer  waits with him  waits with her  waits for him","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v11-p385-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.8: Waiting for Ryūen<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V11 · p.385–388<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Says she does not have time for this. Says she is having fun with Ishizaki and Shiina. Says she is at her limit. Threatens to kick Ryūen’s ass.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ishizaki-daichi.html\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/a> · <a href=\"shiina-hiyori.html\">Shiina Hiyori<\/a> · <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“I don’t have the time for this...”<span class=\"pg\">p.385<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Besides, I’m having tons of fun spending time with you two. Won’t you stay?”<span class=\"pg\">p.386<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I can’t take it anymore! I’m at my limit!”<span class=\"pg\">p.387<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ll kick your ass if you leave me here in karaoke hell any longer.”<span class=\"pg\">p.388<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/b> Waits with him.<span class=\"pg\">p.382–388<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shiina Hiyori<\/b> Waits with her.<span class=\"pg\">p.383–388<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Waits for him.<span class=\"pg\">p.383–388<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v11-p383-1\">← Before: Ch.8: Planning against Class B<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v11_5-p150-1","v":"y1v11.5","y":1,"o":14,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka ishizaki-daichi ryuuen-kakeru ibuki-mio","q":"ibuki mio ch 3  encounter on the way to the mall ibuki encounters ayanokoji in the dormitory elevator and walks toward keyaki mall at the same pace despite her irritation  when ishizaki arrives  ibuki scolds him for letting slip that they are meeting ryuen  she dismisses ishizaki s idea of bringing ayanokoji into class d as impossible  ibuki parts from ayanokoji with ishizaki at keyaki mall  encounters him and reacts negatively to ishizaki s proposal involving him  meets him on the way to see ryuen  is implied to be the person they are going to meet","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v11_5-p150-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3: Encounter on the way to the mall<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V11.5 · p.150–156<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Ibuki encounters Ayanokōji in the dormitory elevator and walks toward Keyaki mall at the same pace despite her irritation. When Ishizaki arrives, Ibuki scolds him for letting slip that they are meeting Ryūen. She dismisses Ishizaki’s idea of bringing Ayanokōji into Class D as impossible. Ibuki parts from Ayanokōji with Ishizaki at Keyaki mall.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"ishizaki-daichi.html\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/a> · <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Encounters him and reacts negatively to Ishizaki’s proposal involving him.<span class=\"pg\">p.150–156<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/b> Meets him on the way to see Ryūen.<span class=\"pg\">p.153–156<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Is implied to be the person they are going to meet.<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v11_5-p387-1\">→ After: Short story: Meeting with Ryūen<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v11_5-p387-1","v":"y1v11.5","y":1,"o":14,"k":"","w":"ryuuen-kakeru ishizaki-daichi ayanokouji-kiyotaka ibuki-mio","q":"ibuki mio short story  meeting with ryuen in ryuen s short story  ibuki meets him at keyaki mall with ishizaki  she dismisses ishizaki s idea of ayanokoji joining forces with ryuen  meets him at the mall  is present with him  reacts to ishizaki s mention of him","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v11_5-p387-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Short story: Meeting with Ryūen<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V11.5 · p.387–388<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">In Ryūen’s short story, Ibuki meets him at Keyaki mall with Ishizaki. She dismisses Ishizaki’s idea of Ayanokōji joining forces with Ryūen.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"ishizaki-daichi.html\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Meets him at the mall.<span class=\"pg\">p.387–388<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/b> Is present with him.<span class=\"pg\">p.387–388<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Reacts to Ishizaki’s mention of him.<span class=\"pg\">p.387<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v11_5-p150-1\">← Before: Ch.3: Encounter on the way to the mall<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y2v1-p87-1","v":"y2v1","y":2,"o":16,"k":"","w":"ryuuen-kakeru ishizaki-daichi housen-kazuomi ibuki-mio","q":"ibuki mio ch 3  class 1 d hallway asks why ryuen stopped ishizaki  is choked by hosen and dropped  is defended by him  argues with him  is attacked by him","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y2v1-p87-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3: Class 1-D hallway<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V1 · p.87, 90–92<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Asks why Ryūen stopped Ishizaki. Is choked by Hōsen and dropped.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"ishizaki-daichi.html\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/a> · <a href=\"housen-kazuomi.html\">Hōsen Kazuomi<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Is defended by him.<span class=\"pg\">p.87–92<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/b> Argues with him.<span class=\"pg\">p.87<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hōsen Kazuomi<\/b> Is attacked by him.<span class=\"pg\">p.90–92<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y2v1-p200-1\">→ After: Ch.4: Karaoke strategy session<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y2v1-p200-1","v":"y2v1","y":2,"o":16,"k":"","w":"ryuuen-kakeru ibuki-mio","q":"ibuki mio ch 4  karaoke strategy session reports class 1 b student put offer on hold  questions ryuen s strategy  discusses strategy with him","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y2v1-p200-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4: Karaoke strategy session<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V1 · p.200–203<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Reports Class 1-B student put offer on hold. Questions Ryūen’s strategy.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Discusses strategy with him.<span class=\"pg\">p.200–203<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y2v1-p87-1\">← Before: Ch.3: Class 1-D hallway<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y2v1-p200-2\">→ After: Ch.5: Strategy session<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y2v1-p200-2","v":"y2v1","y":2,"o":16,"k":"","w":"ryuuen-kakeru ibuki-mio","q":"ibuki mio ch 5  strategy session reports class 1 b student put offer on hold  questions ryuen s strategy  discusses strategy with him","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y2v1-p200-2\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.5: Strategy session<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V1 · p.200–203<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Reports Class 1-B student put offer on hold. Questions Ryūen’s strategy.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Discusses strategy with him.<span class=\"pg\">p.200–203<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y2v1-p200-1\">← Before: Ch.4: Karaoke strategy session<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y2v1-p200-3\">→ After: Epilogue: Strategy session<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y2v1-p200-3","v":"y2v1","y":2,"o":16,"k":"","w":"ryuuen-kakeru ibuki-mio","q":"ibuki mio epilogue  strategy session reports class 1 b student put offer on hold  questions ryuen s strategy  discusses strategy with him","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y2v1-p200-3\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Epilogue: Strategy session<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V1 · p.200–203<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Reports Class 1-B student put offer on hold. Questions Ryūen’s strategy.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Discusses strategy with him.<span class=\"pg\">p.200–203<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y2v1-p200-2\">← Before: Ch.5: Strategy session<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y2v1-p311-1\">→ After: Ch.6: Mention<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y2v1-p311-1","v":"y2v1","y":2,"o":16,"k":"","w":"ibuki-mio","q":"ibuki mio ch 6  mention mentioned as class 2 c student","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y2v1-p311-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6: Mention<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V1 · p.311<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Mentioned as Class 2-C student.<\/p><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y2v1-p200-3\">← Before: Epilogue: Strategy session<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y2v2-p163-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"","w":"ibuki-mio","q":"ibuki mio ibuki mentioned in passing named in the ryuen alliance meeting context  named in the ryuen katsuragi negotiation  passing mentions  not a distinct scene presence  passing mention only","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y2v2-p163-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ibuki mentioned in passing<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.163, 188, 315–325<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named in the Ryūen alliance meeting context. Named in the Ryūen-Katsuragi negotiation.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Passing mentions; not a distinct scene presence.<span class=\"pg\">p.163, 188, 315–325<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> Passing mention only.<span class=\"pg\">p.163, 188, 315–325<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y2v3-p14-1","v":"y2v3","y":2,"o":18,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka kitou-hayato ibuki-mio","q":"ibuki mio ibuki at the briefing  stuck beside ayanokoji  ugh  why the hell are you sitting here   you didn t sit there on purpose  right   i m goin  somewhere else  so don t you dare follow me  got it  tries to leave the back seat when ayanokoji sits beside her  but kito takes her escape seat and the groups fill the rest  grudgingly stays  sandwiched between kito and myself    she d rather tolerate him than join a group  having chosen to take the exam alone  refuses to follow him  forced to sit beside him anyway  takes the seat she wanted  glowering at him as he folds his arms","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y2v3-p14-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ibuki at the briefing, stuck beside Ayanokōji<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V3 · p.14–16<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"kitou-hayato.html\">Kitō Hayato<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;…Ugh. Why the hell are you sitting here?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;You didn&#x27;t sit there on purpose, right?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I&#x27;m goin&#x27; somewhere else, so don&#x27;t you dare follow me, got it?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Tries to leave the back seat when Ayanokōji sits beside her, but Kitō takes her escape seat and the groups fill the rest; grudgingly stays &quot;sandwiched between Kitō and myself&quot; — she&#x27;d rather tolerate him than join a group, having chosen to take the exam alone.<span class=\"pg\">p.14–16<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Refuses to follow him; forced to sit beside him anyway.<span class=\"pg\">p.15–16<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kitō Hayato<\/b> Takes the seat she wanted, glowering at him as he folds his arms.<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y2v4-p5-1","v":"y2v4","y":2,"o":19,"k":"","w":"ibuki-mio","q":"ibuki mio full volume appears in this volume","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y2v4-p5-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Full volume<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V4 · p.5-284<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Appears in this volume.<\/p><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y2v4-p67-1\">→ After: Ibuki alone and dehydrated; trades with Ayanokōji<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y2v4-p67-1","v":"y2v4","y":2,"o":19,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-suzune ibuki-mio","q":"ibuki mio ibuki alone and dehydrated  trades with ayanokoji encountered alone  eating homemade jerky  class 2 b s jerky strategy    exhausted  dark circles  out of water for over a day   what s it matter to you  it s none of your business   just horikita  you heard me say i wouldn t lose to her  right   ain t no way i m gonna talk with my enemies   i don t think of my classmates as  friends   how many points you got right now   when you next see that bitch  do me a solid and tell her that i ll absolutely never lose to her   haaa  you tryna pull somethin   i ll admit i can t beat you  sure  but one of these days  i swear i m gonna get the satisfaction of kickin  your teeth in   a full day  and then some   i ll handle it tomorrow  and if push comes to shove i ll even go back to the starting area  so drop it and leave me alone   i m not gonna thank you if that s what you re after   so you re sayin  for me to give up on scoring points  you ve gotta be kidding me   i m not puttin  in all this work  cause i don t wanna get expelled  my only goal here is beating horikita  stubborn  isolated and pushing past her limits   refuses to admit dehydration or rest  suspicious of ayanokoji  thinks horikita put him up to it  but ultimately trades half her food for water  driven solely by her obsession with beating horikita  she rejects his advice to rest  her guardedness and irrationality are slowly destroying her  deeply suspicious of him  but accepts the water for food trade  misreads his concern as manipulation  her obsession and sole goal   to beat horikita  whom she calls a  bitch","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y2v4-p67-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ibuki alone and dehydrated; trades with Ayanokōji<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V4 · p.67–78<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Encountered alone, eating homemade jerky (Class 2-B&#x27;s jerky strategy) — exhausted, dark circles, out of water for over a day.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;What&#x27;s it matter to you? It&#x27;s none of your business.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.67<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Just Horikita. You heard me say I wouldn&#x27;t lose to her, right?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.68<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Ain&#x27;t no way I&#x27;m gonna talk with my enemies.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.68<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>13 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I don&#x27;t think of my classmates as &#x27;friends&#x27;.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.68<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;How many points you got right now?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.70<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;When you next see that bitch, do me a solid and tell her that I&#x27;ll absolutely never lose to her.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.71<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Haaa? You tryna pull somethin&#x27;?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I&#x27;ll admit I can&#x27;t beat you, sure, but one of these days, I swear I&#x27;m gonna get the satisfaction of kickin&#x27; your teeth in.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;…A full day… and then some.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I&#x27;ll handle it tomorrow, and if push comes to shove I&#x27;ll even go back to the starting area, so drop it and leave me alone.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I&#x27;m not gonna thank you if that&#x27;s what you&#x27;re after.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.77<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;So you&#x27;re sayin&#x27; for me to give up on scoring points? You&#x27;ve gotta be kidding me.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.77<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I&#x27;m not puttin&#x27; in all this work &#x27;cause I don&#x27;t wanna get expelled. My only goal here is beating Horikita.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.77<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Stubborn, isolated and pushing past her limits — refuses to admit dehydration or rest, suspicious of Ayanokōji (thinks Horikita put him up to it), but ultimately trades half her food for water; driven solely by her obsession with beating Horikita, she rejects his advice to rest; her guardedness and irrationality are slowly destroying her.<span class=\"pg\">p.67–78<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Deeply suspicious of him, but accepts the water-for-food trade; misreads his concern as manipulation.<span class=\"pg\">p.67–78<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Her obsession and sole goal — to beat Horikita, whom she calls a &quot;bitch.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.68–77<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y2v4-p5-1\">← Before: Full volume<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y2v4_5-p10-1","v":"y2v4.5","y":2,"o":20,"k":"","w":"ibuki-mio","q":"ibuki mio full volume appears in this volume","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y2v4_5-p10-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Full volume<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V4.5 · p.10-290<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Appears in this volume.<\/p><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y2v5-p7-1","v":"y2v5","y":2,"o":21,"k":"","w":"ibuki-mio","q":"ibuki mio full volume appears in this volume","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y2v5-p7-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Full volume<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V5 · p.7-243<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Appears in this volume.<\/p><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y2v6-p11-1","v":"y2v6","y":2,"o":22,"k":"","w":"ibuki-mio","q":"ibuki mio full volume appears in this volume","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y2v6-p11-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Full volume<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V6 · p.11-346<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Appears in this volume.<\/p><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y2v6-p112-1\">→ After: Ibuki: the cryptic message; breaking into Kushida&#x27;s room<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y2v6-p112-1","v":"y2v6","y":2,"o":22,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-suzune kushida-kikyou ibuki-mio","q":"ibuki mio ibuki  the cryptic message  breaking into kushida s room corners ayanokoji at the dorm elevator  shoving her phone at him over a message he sent  if you get expelled because of something that has nothing to do with me  naturally  it will count as a loss against me    she spent a week trying to understand it   just how is this intelligent  no  forget it  just tell me what it means   i m gonna force kushida out of her room  this will be all or nothing   i ve never thought positively of you even once    to kushida  you guys gonna keep this up until you ve ripped each other apart  you look fucking stupid so i m going home  blunt and impatient   couldn t parse ayanokoji s warning not to be manipulated into expulsion  chosen by horikita to break the deadlock  she mashes kushida s doorbell  forces the door open and curses her out  venting her own stress at horikita  calls out the absurd cheek pinching contest between horikita and kushida and leaves   ayanokoji notes her  talent to annoy people  made the meeting possible  he sent her a cryptic warning  she demands an explanation  she helped her get into kushida s room but has no patience for their antics  she berates her and forces her door open    i ve never thought positively of you","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y2v6-p112-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ibuki: the cryptic message; breaking into Kushida&#x27;s room<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V6 · p.112–145<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Corners Ayanokōji at the dorm elevator, shoving her phone at him over a message he sent (&quot;If you get expelled because of something that has nothing to do with me, naturally, it will count as a loss against me&quot;) — she spent a week trying to understand it.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Just how is this intelligent? No, forget it, just tell me what it means!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I&#x27;m gonna force Kushida out of her room. This will be all or nothing.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.123<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I&#x27;ve never thought positively of you even once.&quot; — to Kushida<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You guys gonna keep this up until you&#x27;ve ripped each other apart? You look fucking stupid so I&#x27;m going home.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.145<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Blunt and impatient — couldn&#x27;t parse Ayanokōji&#x27;s warning not to be manipulated into expulsion; chosen by Horikita to break the deadlock, she mashes Kushida&#x27;s doorbell, forces the door open and curses her out (venting her own stress at Horikita); calls out the absurd cheek-pinching contest between Horikita and Kushida and leaves — Ayanokōji notes her &quot;talent to annoy people&quot; made the meeting possible.<span class=\"pg\">p.112–145<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> He sent her a cryptic warning; she demands an explanation.<span class=\"pg\">p.112–113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> She helped her get into Kushida&#x27;s room but has no patience for their antics.<span class=\"pg\">p.145<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> She berates her and forces her door open — &quot;I&#x27;ve never thought positively of you.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.121–125<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y2v6-p11-1\">← Before: Full volume<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y2v6-p243-1\">→ After: Ibuki: the endless duel with Horikita<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y2v6-p243-1","v":"y2v6","y":2,"o":22,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune amasawa-ichika ibuki-mio","q":"ibuki mio ibuki  the endless duel with horikita  come  horikita  fight me   huh  what are you saying  you scared of losing to me  you are  aren t you   i did it     did you see  i won  you lose   1 win  1 loss  we haven t settled this yet   then i ll participate too  at any rate  you won t be able to get five players   teaming up with you sucks  but this is a chance to beat that piece of shit brat of a first year  obsessed with settling their rivalry   sprints up exhausted before the 100m  loses by the same narrow margin as last year  beats horikita in the long jump by 2cm  5 81m  then misses the balance beam registration  a default loss  badgers horikita until she begs  pl ease  fight  me  then joins her volleyball team purely to crush amasawa   her competitive fire and inability to let go are both endearing and exhausting  her rival   they re 1 1 after the long jump  and she refuses to let the score stand  horikita notes she has no friends but agrees to team up  she wants to beat the  piece of shit brat  first year   joins horikita s volleyball team for that chance","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y2v6-p243-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ibuki: the endless duel with Horikita<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V6 · p.243–275<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"amasawa-ichika.html\">Amasawa Ichika<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Come, Horikita! Fight me!!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.243<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Huh?! What are you saying? You scared of losing to me? You are, aren&#x27;t you?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.243<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I did it!&quot; / &quot;Did you see? I won! You lose!!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.248<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;1 Win, 1 Loss! We haven&#x27;t settled this yet!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.269<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Then I&#x27;ll participate too. At any rate, you won&#x27;t be able to get five players.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.271<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Teaming up with you sucks, but this is a chance to beat that piece of shit brat of a first year!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.275<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Obsessed with settling their rivalry — sprints up exhausted before the 100m, loses by the same narrow margin as last year, beats Horikita in the long jump by 2cm (5.81m), then misses the balance-beam registration (a default loss); badgers Horikita until she begs (&quot;Pl…ease… fight… me!!&quot;), then joins her volleyball team purely to crush Amasawa — her competitive fire and inability to let go are both endearing and exhausting.<span class=\"pg\">p.243–275<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Her rival — they&#x27;re 1–1 after the long jump, and she refuses to let the score stand; Horikita notes she has no friends but agrees to team up.<span class=\"pg\">p.243–275<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Amasawa Ichika<\/b> She wants to beat the &quot;piece of shit brat&quot; first-year — joins Horikita&#x27;s volleyball team for that chance.<span class=\"pg\">p.273–275<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y2v6-p112-1\">← Before: Ibuki: the cryptic message; breaking into Kushida&#x27;s room<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y2v7-p7-1","v":"y2v7","y":2,"o":23,"k":"","w":"ibuki-mio","q":"ibuki mio full volume appears in this volume","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y2v7-p7-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Full volume<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V7 · p.7-207<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Appears in this volume.<\/p><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y2v8-p11-1","v":"y2v8","y":2,"o":24,"k":"","w":"ibuki-mio","q":"ibuki mio full volume appears in this volume","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y2v8-p11-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Full volume<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V8 · p.11-208<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Appears in this volume.<\/p><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y2v9_75-p4-1","v":"y2v9.75","y":2,"o":27,"k":"","w":"ibuki-mio","q":"ibuki mio full volume appears in this volume","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y2v9_75-p4-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Full volume<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V9.75 · p.4-8<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Appears in this volume.<\/p><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y2v10-p9-1","v":"y2v10","y":2,"o":28,"k":"","w":"ibuki-mio","q":"ibuki mio full volume appears in this volume","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y2v10-p9-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Full volume<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V10 · p.9-235<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Appears in this volume.<\/p><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y2v11-p11-1","v":"y2v11","y":2,"o":30,"k":"","w":"ibuki-mio","q":"ibuki mio full volume appears in this volume","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y2v11-p11-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Full volume<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V11 · p.11-223<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Appears in this volume.<\/p><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y2v12_5-p80-1","v":"y2v12.5","y":2,"o":32,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka ibuki-mio","q":"ibuki mio ch 5  ch 9 mentioned appears in ch 5  ch 9  appears in this volume","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y2v12_5-p80-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.5, Ch.9<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V12.5 · p.80-84, 148-157<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Mentioned/appears in Ch.5, Ch.9.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Appears in this volume.<span class=\"pg\">p.80-84, 148-157<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y3v1-p136-1","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-suzune ishizaki-daichi ibuki-mio","q":"ibuki mio ibuki s disdain and horikita s cooking  why are you asking me  just do what you want   why not just give up  losing the opportunity to gain about a hundred class points isn t a big deal  right   i don t care about that story   don t ask me  you shouldn t even try to understand his thoughts   i get really annoyed just talking about him  i truly hate him   it s annoying   haaaaaaa  she s not my friend  combative and blunt   recommends giving up the academic exam  refuses to engage with ayanokoji  having learned it leads to complications  genuinely hates him  and denies being horikita s friend despite eating at her room  refuses to think about him  says she truly hates him  has been coming to her room for food but says they aren t friends  notes she hasn t recovered  bickers with him over food and ayanokoji","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y3v1-p136-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ibuki&#x27;s disdain and Horikita&#x27;s cooking<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.136–143<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"ishizaki-daichi.html\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Why are you asking me? Just do what you want.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.136<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Why not just give up? Losing the opportunity to gain about a hundred class points isn&#x27;t a big deal, right?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.136<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I don&#x27;t care about that story.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.137<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Don&#x27;t ask me. You shouldn&#x27;t even try to understand his thoughts.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.137<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I get really annoyed just talking about him. I truly hate him.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.138<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;It&#x27;s annoying.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.142<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Haaaaaaa? She&#x27;s not my friend.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.142<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Combative and blunt — recommends giving up the academic exam, refuses to engage with Ayanokōji (having learned it leads to complications), genuinely hates him, and denies being Horikita&#x27;s friend despite eating at her room.<span class=\"pg\">p.136–143<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Refuses to think about him; says she truly hates him.<span class=\"pg\">p.137–138<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Has been coming to her room for food but says they aren&#x27;t friends; notes she hasn&#x27;t recovered.<span class=\"pg\">p.142<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/b> Bickers with him over food and Ayanokōji.<span class=\"pg\">p.136–138<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y3v1-p203-1\">→ After: Ch.8 — depth read: Ibuki&#x27;s blunt &quot;concern&quot;<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y3v1-p203-1","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka karuizawa-kei ibuki-mio","q":"ibuki mio ch 8   depth read  ibuki s blunt  concern  kicks horikita in the back from behind on the gravel path outside the dorm   you ve grown pathetic  horikita  you can t even dodge a kick like that   your pathetic appearance has always been irritating to me  it pisses me off just looking at you   i d jump for joy  just seeing his face makes me so angry   if you plan to stay this pathetic forever  i m done with you  don t ever get involved with me again  blunt and violent  but the chapter hints  through karuizawa  that she may have been worried in her own way   she lingered near the bench rather than going home  kicks her for being pathetic since ayanokoji s departure and tells her to stay out of her sight  is irritated that he defeated ryuen and angry just thinking about him  has been coming to horikita  and previously karuizawa  for food  karuizawa speculates ibuki s anger and lingering may be a rough form of concern for horikita","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y3v1-p203-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.8 — depth read: Ibuki&#x27;s blunt &quot;concern&quot;<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.203–224<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Kicks Horikita in the back from behind on the gravel path outside the dorm.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;You&#x27;ve grown pathetic, Horikita. You can&#x27;t even dodge a kick like that.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Your pathetic appearance has always been irritating to me. It pisses me off just looking at you.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.208<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I&#x27;d jump for joy. Just seeing his face makes me so angry.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.208<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;If you plan to stay this pathetic forever, I&#x27;m done with you. Don&#x27;t ever get involved with me again.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.208<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Blunt and violent, but the chapter hints (through Karuizawa) that she may have been worried in her own way — she lingered near the bench rather than going home.<span class=\"pg\">p.207–208<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Kicks her for being pathetic since Ayanokōji&#x27;s departure and tells her to stay out of her sight.<span class=\"pg\">p.207–208<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Is irritated that he defeated Ryūen and angry just thinking about him.<span class=\"pg\">p.208<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Has been coming to Horikita (and previously Karuizawa) for food.<span class=\"pg\">p.211, per Karuizawa<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Karuizawa speculates Ibuki&#x27;s anger and lingering may be a rough form of concern for Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.208<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y3v1-p136-1\">← Before: Ibuki&#x27;s disdain and Horikita&#x27;s cooking<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y3v1-p207-1\">→ After: Ibuki kicks Horikita out of frustration<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y3v1-p207-1","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka ryuuen-kakeru ibuki-mio","q":"ibuki mio ibuki kicks horikita out of frustration finds horikita walking alone on the gravel outside the dorm after the exam and kicks her hard in the back without warning   you ve grown pathetic  horikita  you can t even dodge a kick like that   your pathetic appearance has always been irritating to me  it pisses me off just looking at you   see  that s what i mean  that kind of spineless attitude keeps jumping into my line of sight  it can t be helped  you should be thankful i only kicked you   everyone s always going off about ayanokouji this  ayanokouji that  can t you be glad that the plague is finally gone from your class   i d jump for joy  just seeing his face makes me so angry  ah  just thinking about it makes me angry   if you plan to stay this pathetic forever  i m done with you  don t ever get involved with me again  in fact  don t even come into my sight  combative and foul tempered   kicks a defenseless horikita in frustration  insists it had not one percent of malice  vents that ayanokoji s departure should be celebrated but it was ryuen who got embarrassed  and storms off  she had been lingering by the bench as if waiting for someone   possibly worried about horikita in her own rough way  though horikita dismisses the notion  kicks her  calls her pathetic  and orders her to stay out of her sight  she had helped ibuki when she was short on cash but was never thanked  enraged at the mere thought of him  claims she d  jump for joy  at his leaving  bitter that it was ryuen  not ayanokoji  who ended up embarrassed in the exam","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y3v1-p207-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ibuki kicks Horikita out of frustration<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.207–208<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Finds Horikita walking alone on the gravel outside the dorm after the exam and kicks her hard in the back without warning.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;You&#x27;ve grown pathetic, Horikita. You can&#x27;t even dodge a kick like that.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Your pathetic appearance has always been irritating to me. It pisses me off just looking at you.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;See, that&#x27;s what I mean. That kind of spineless attitude keeps jumping into my line of sight; it can&#x27;t be helped. You should be thankful I only kicked you.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.208<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Everyone&#x27;s always going off about Ayanokouji this, Ayanokouji that. Can&#x27;t you be glad that the plague is finally gone from your class?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.208<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I&#x27;d jump for joy. Just seeing his face makes me so angry… Ah, just thinking about it makes me angry.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.208<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;If you plan to stay this pathetic forever, I&#x27;m done with you. Don&#x27;t ever get involved with me again, in fact, don&#x27;t even come into my sight.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.208<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Combative and foul-tempered — kicks a defenseless Horikita in frustration, insists it had not one percent of malice, vents that Ayanokōji&#x27;s departure should be celebrated but it was Ryūen who got embarrassed, and storms off.<span class=\"pg\">p.207–208<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> She had been lingering by the bench as if waiting for someone — possibly worried about Horikita in her own rough way, though Horikita dismisses the notion.<span class=\"pg\">p.211<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Kicks her, calls her pathetic, and orders her to stay out of her sight; she had helped Ibuki when she was short on cash but was never thanked.<span class=\"pg\">p.207–208<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Enraged at the mere thought of him; claims she&#x27;d &quot;jump for joy&quot; at his leaving.<span class=\"pg\">p.208<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Bitter that it was Ryūen, not Ayanokōji, who ended up embarrassed in the exam.<span class=\"pg\">p.208<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y3v1-p203-1\">← Before: Ch.8 — depth read: Ibuki&#x27;s blunt &quot;concern&quot;<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y3v1-p257-1\">→ After: &quot;Behind the Scenes, Part 1&quot;: resisting the comfort of Horikita&#x27;s room<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y3v1-p257-1","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"narration","w":"horikita-suzune kushida-kikyou ibuki-mio","q":"ibuki mio  behind the scenes  part 1  resisting the comfort of horikita s room flops on the floor of horikita s room  staring at the ceiling  resolving that she should stop coming for the free meals before she grows too close   if it weren t for the free meals  i wouldn t have come to a place like this  secretly admits she has come to see horikita and kushida s room as a  comfortable space  and that she is getting closer to people she detests  decides to distance herself   until the smell of food makes her forget the resolve  enjoys her cooking but tells herself she should leave before growing attached  also growing closer to her despite detesting her","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y3v1-p257-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">&quot;Behind the Scenes, Part 1&quot;: resisting the comfort of Horikita&#x27;s room<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.257<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Flops on the floor of Horikita&#x27;s room, staring at the ceiling, resolving that she should stop coming for the free meals before she grows too close.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;If it weren&#x27;t for the free meals, I wouldn&#x27;t have come to a place like this…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.257<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Secretly admits she has come to see Horikita and Kushida&#x27;s room as a &quot;comfortable space&quot; and that she is getting closer to people she detests; decides to distance herself — until the smell of food makes her forget the resolve.<span class=\"pg\">p.257<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Enjoys her cooking but tells herself she should leave before growing attached.<span class=\"pg\">p.257<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Also growing closer to her despite detesting her.<span class=\"pg\">p.257<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y3v1-p207-1\">← Before: Ibuki kicks Horikita out of frustration<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y3v1-p265-1\">→ After: &quot;Concern?&quot;: the impulse behind the kick<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y3v1-p265-1","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"narration","w":"horikita-suzune katsuragi-kouhei ayanokouji-kiyotaka ibuki-mio","q":"ibuki mio  concern  the impulse behind the kick paces near the school entrance after school  waiting for horikita  irritated that the free meals have stopped and that horikita has been dejected since ayanokoji s transfer   come out already  how concerned do you plan to make  no  no  i m not concerned  cannot admit she is worried   pushes the feeling away as odd thinking from not having eaten well  recalls katsuragi s advice that a person should only be kicked if they would benefit from it  and acts on impulse when horikita emerges lifeless  waits over half an hour for her  then delivers the  merciless kick  in ch 8   framed here as a rough attempt to snap her out of her depression and get meals again  recalls his words about when it is permissible to kick someone  secretly pleased at his transfer and at ryuen s strategy being seen through  but the greater frustration is horikita s state","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y3v1-p265-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">&quot;Concern?&quot;: the impulse behind the kick<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.265–266<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Paces near the school entrance after school, waiting for Horikita, irritated that the free meals have stopped and that Horikita has been dejected since Ayanokōji&#x27;s transfer.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;Come out already. How concerned do you plan to make… no, no, I&#x27;m not concerned.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.266<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Cannot admit she is worried — pushes the feeling away as odd thinking from not having eaten well; recalls Katsuragi&#x27;s advice that a person should only be kicked if they would benefit from it, and acts on impulse when Horikita emerges lifeless.<span class=\"pg\">p.265–266<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Waits over half an hour for her, then delivers the &quot;merciless kick&quot; in Ch.8 — framed here as a rough attempt to snap her out of her depression and get meals again.<span class=\"pg\">p.265–266<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> Recalls his words about when it is permissible to kick someone.<span class=\"pg\">p.266<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Secretly pleased at his transfer and at Ryūen&#x27;s strategy being seen through, but the greater frustration is Horikita&#x27;s state.<span class=\"pg\">p.265<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y3v1-p257-1\">← Before: &quot;Behind the Scenes, Part 1&quot;: resisting the comfort of Horikita&#x27;s room<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y3v2-p66-1","v":"y3v2","y":3,"o":34,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune ibuki-mio","q":"ibuki mio ch 3   depth read  ibuki s meal and the kick warning comes to horikita s room after 6 30 pm for a meal  after the flying kick she gave her earlier   for a loser  your color s looking a little better  horikita   if it happens again  i ll be sure to kick you then  too  so be grateful  blunt and sarcastic  takes horikita s thanks as praise and laughs off the warning about kicking her in the back  eats at her room  warned not to kick people in the back again  horikita notes ibuki ate every grain of rice  but left a mess   a clue toward the  daily conduct  theory","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y3v2-p66-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3 — depth read: Ibuki&#x27;s meal and the kick warning<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V2 · p.66–125<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Comes to Horikita&#x27;s room after 6:30 PM for a meal (after the flying kick she gave her earlier).<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;For a loser, your color&#x27;s looking a little better, Horikita.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;If it happens again, I&#x27;ll be sure to kick you then, too, so be grateful.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Blunt and sarcastic; takes Horikita&#x27;s thanks as praise and laughs off the warning about kicking her in the back.<span class=\"pg\">p.94–95<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Eats at her room; warned not to kick people in the back again.<span class=\"pg\">p.94–95<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Horikita notes Ibuki ate every grain of rice, but left a mess — a clue toward the &quot;daily conduct&quot; theory.<span class=\"pg\">p.95<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y3v2-p96-1\">→ After: Ibuki at the dinner: Ayanokōji is impossible to beat<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y3v2-p96-1","v":"y3v2","y":3,"o":34,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka kushida-kikyou ibuki-mio","q":"ibuki mio ibuki at the dinner  ayanokoji is impossible to beat eats the wagyu meal enthusiastically in horikita s room   huh  what  what  why are you trying to pick a fight all of a sudden   savage   beat ayanokouji  huh  that s impossible   he s as strong as a monster and surprise attacks don t work on him   neither you nor i could even touch him  even that albert guy was like a kid in front of ayanokouji   you re useless  aren t ya   that guy was already a monster back in the winter of our first year  combative and blunt   enjoys the free meal  i ve been flat broke lately  admits defeat against ayanokoji outright  and calls horikita useless for not knowing the secret to his strength  argues with kushida throughout  considers him unbeatable  a  monster  already in their first year  bickers with her  calling her an  idiot  both restrain themselves from fighting in horikita s room","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y3v2-p96-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ibuki at the dinner: Ayanokōji is impossible to beat<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V2 · p.96–110<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Eats the wagyu meal enthusiastically in Horikita&#x27;s room.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Huh? What, what? Why are you trying to pick a fight all of a sudden?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.96<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Savage.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.99<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Beat Ayanokouji, huh? That&#x27;s impossible.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.101<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;He&#x27;s as strong as a monster and surprise attacks don&#x27;t work on him.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.101<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Neither you nor I could even touch him. Even that Albert guy was like a kid in front of Ayanokouji.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.102<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You&#x27;re useless, aren&#x27;t ya.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.102<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;That guy was already a monster back in the winter of our first year.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.103<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Combative and blunt — enjoys the free meal (&quot;I&#x27;ve been flat broke lately&quot;), admits defeat against Ayanokōji outright, and calls Horikita useless for not knowing the secret to his strength; argues with Kushida throughout.<span class=\"pg\">p.96–110<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Considers him unbeatable, a &quot;monster&quot; already in their first year.<span class=\"pg\">p.101–103<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Bickers with her, calling her an &quot;idiot&quot;; both restrain themselves from fighting in Horikita&#x27;s room.<span class=\"pg\">p.96–110<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y3v2-p66-1\">← Before: Ch.3 — depth read: Ibuki&#x27;s meal and the kick warning<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y3v3-p131-1","v":"y3v3","y":3,"o":35,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka ryuuen-kakeru morofuji-rika ibuki-mio","q":"ibuki mio depth review  the wild card eliminated ambushes a class b supply group surrounding morofuji  unseen  eliminating eight guards in under thirty seconds   die  ayanokouji   agh  dammit  so this is how it ends  single handedly picks off eight class b guards with precise submachine gun fire from cover  cocky and theatrical   thanks her victims for the fun  calls the encounter  an act of kindness  in koenji s own way  fiercely competitive  loud and profane when she loses  is hit by ayanokoji s final shot to the right thigh after her own spray runs dry  eliminated  complains she never wanted to take part in the exam  fights him alongside ryuen at the end  partners with him in the final 2 v 1  spares her and lets class b keep the supplies","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y3v3-p131-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Depth review: the wild card eliminated<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V3 · p.131–240<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Ambushes a Class B supply group surrounding Morofuji, unseen, eliminating eight guards in under thirty seconds.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"morofuji-rika.html\">Morofuji Rika<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Die, Ayanokouji!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.238<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Agh, dammit! So this is how it ends!?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.240<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Single-handedly picks off eight Class B guards with precise submachine-gun fire from cover.<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Voice<\/span> Cocky and theatrical — thanks her victims for the fun, calls the encounter &quot;an act of kindness, in Koenji&#x27;s own way.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Fiercely competitive, loud and profane when she loses.<span class=\"pg\">p.240<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> Is hit by Ayanokōji&#x27;s final shot to the right thigh after her own spray runs dry.<span class=\"pg\">p.240<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Eliminated; complains she never wanted to take part in the exam.<span class=\"pg\">p.240<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Fights him alongside Ryūen at the end.<span class=\"pg\">p.236–240<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Partners with him in the final 2-v-1.<span class=\"pg\">p.236–240<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Morofuji Rika<\/b> Spares her and lets Class B keep the supplies.<span class=\"pg\">p.131–134<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y3v3-p212-1\">→ After: Ibuki&#x27;s grudge against Horikita<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y3v3-p212-1","v":"y3v3","y":3,"o":35,"k":"spoken","w":"ishizaki-daichi horikita-suzune ibuki-mio","q":"ibuki mio ibuki s grudge against horikita breaks into a fierce smile on learning class a is behind them   because i ve finally met the opponent i m supposed to take down   i ve just been itching for a fight  because i wanted so  so badly to see that look of frustration on that horikita girl s face   all my pent up grudges  i m gonna pay them back right here  right now   you re my support   as long as i can take down horikita  that s all that matters  ferocious and single minded   cares nothing for the exam s result  only for beating horikita  and drags ishizaki in as her shield to charge the enemy  forces him to be her shield  they charge together  obsessed with seeing the look of frustration on horikita s face","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y3v3-p212-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ibuki&#x27;s grudge against Horikita<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V3 · p.212–215<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Breaks into a fierce smile on learning Class A is behind them.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ishizaki-daichi.html\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Because I&#x27;ve finally met the opponent I&#x27;m supposed to take down.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.212<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I&#x27;ve just been itching for a fight... because I wanted so, so badly to see that look of frustration on that Horikita girl&#x27;s face!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.213<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;All my pent-up grudges, I&#x27;m gonna pay them back right here, right now!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.215<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You&#x27;re my support.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.215<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;As long as I can take down Horikita, that&#x27;s all that matters!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.215<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Ferocious and single-minded — cares nothing for the exam&#x27;s result, only for beating Horikita, and drags Ishizaki in as her shield to charge the enemy.<span class=\"pg\">p.212–215<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/b> Forces him to be her shield; they charge together.<span class=\"pg\">p.215<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Obsessed with seeing the look of frustration on Horikita&#x27;s face.<span class=\"pg\">p.213–215<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y3v3-p131-1\">← Before: Depth review: the wild card eliminated<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y3v3-p233-1\">→ After: Epilogue — depth read: the wild card falls<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y3v3-p233-1","v":"y3v3","y":3,"o":35,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka ryuuen-kakeru ibuki-mio","q":"ibuki mio epilogue   depth read  the wild card falls emerges from the trees beside ryuen to confront ayanokoji in the final shrinking area   die  ayanokouji   where are you even aiming  you think you re gonna hit me with a shot that pathetic  you re a lousy shot   agh  dammit  so this is how it ends  this is so fucking annoying  i told you i didn t want to do this  suppresses ayanokoji with a submachine gun spray and runs between the trees with animal like speed  but is eliminated by a paintball to the right thigh when she misreads his aim  ferocious and impatient   relishes the frontal fight  taunts her opponent  and rages at being eliminated in a game she never wanted to play  is outmaneuvered and eliminated by him  ryuen reveals she had wanted to gamble everything on a shot at a class d vip rather than the 2 v 1","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y3v3-p233-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Epilogue — depth read: the wild card falls<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V3 · p.233–252<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Emerges from the trees beside Ryūen to confront Ayanokōji in the final shrinking area.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Die, Ayanokouji!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.238<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Where are you even aiming? You think you&#x27;re gonna hit me with a shot that pathetic? You&#x27;re a lousy shot.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.239<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Agh, dammit! So this is how it ends!? This is so fucking annoying!! I told you I didn&#x27;t want to do this!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.240<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Suppresses Ayanokōji with a submachine-gun spray and runs between the trees with animal-like speed, but is eliminated by a paintball to the right thigh when she misreads his aim.<span class=\"pg\">p.238–240<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Ferocious and impatient — relishes the frontal fight, taunts her opponent, and rages at being eliminated in a game she never wanted to play.<span class=\"pg\">p.236–240<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Is outmaneuvered and eliminated by him.<span class=\"pg\">p.236–240<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Ryūen reveals she had wanted to gamble everything on a shot at a Class D VIP rather than the 2-v-1.<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y3v3-p212-1\">← Before: Ibuki&#x27;s grudge against Horikita<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y3v3-p236-1\">→ After: Ibuki&#x27;s last stand and elimination<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y3v3-p236-1","v":"y3v3","y":3,"o":35,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka ibuki-mio","q":"ibuki mio ibuki s last stand and elimination  die  ayanokouji   where are you even aiming  you think you re gonna hit me with a shot that pathetic  you re a lousy shot   agh  dammit  so this is how it ends  this is so fucking annoying  i told you i didn t want to do this  suppresses ayanokoji with a submachine gun spray and moves between the trees with animal speed  but is eliminated by a paintball to the thigh when she misreads his aim  ferocious and impatient   relishes the frontal fight  taunts her opponent  and rages at being eliminated  is outmaneuvered and eliminated by him","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y3v3-p236-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ibuki&#x27;s last stand and elimination<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V3 · p.236–240<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Die, Ayanokouji!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.238<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Where are you even aiming? You think you&#x27;re gonna hit me with a shot that pathetic? You&#x27;re a lousy shot.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.239<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Agh, dammit! So this is how it ends!? This is so fucking annoying!! I told you I didn&#x27;t want to do this!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.240<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Suppresses Ayanokōji with a submachine-gun spray and moves between the trees with animal speed, but is eliminated by a paintball to the thigh when she misreads his aim.<span class=\"pg\">p.238–240<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Ferocious and impatient — relishes the frontal fight, taunts her opponent, and rages at being eliminated.<span class=\"pg\">p.236–240<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Is outmaneuvered and eliminated by him.<span class=\"pg\">p.238–240<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y3v3-p233-1\">← Before: Epilogue — depth read: the wild card falls<\/button><\/div><\/article>"}];
